 in the liver and other organs. However, Wilson's disease typically presents in younger individuals and would not explain the patient's negative hepatitis tests.\n\nBased on the patient's symptoms, lab findings, and the analysis of the answer choices, the most likely additional finding in this patient is:\n\nB) Cutaneous xanthomas",
