                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the problem\nThe problem is that the patient's mother is concerned about her son's frequent masturbation and wants to know if there is a problem.\n\nStep 2: Gather more information\nThe patient is a 15-year-old boy who is the captain of his high school wrestling team and does reasonably well in school. On examination, he seems embarrassed and avoids making eye contact. Physical examination shows no abnormalities.\n\nStep 3: Consider the options\nA) Advise the patient to stop masturbating - This is not a helpful or appropriate response. Masturbation is a normal and healthy part of sexual development.\nB) Measure serum testosterone level - This is not necessary in this case as there are no indications of hormonal imbalances.\nC) Refer the patient for behavioral therapy - This may be a helpful option if the patient is experiencing distress or if there are underlying psychological issues contributing to his behavior.\nD) Reassure the mother - This is a good option as it can help alleviate the mother's concerns and provide support for the patient.\nE) Prescribe sertraline - This is not necessary in this case as there are no indications of a psychiatric disorder.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best option\nThe most appropriate next step in management is to reassure the mother. Masturbation is a normal and healthy part of sexual development, and it is important to provide support and education to both the patient and his mother. Referral for behavioral therapy may also be considered if there are underlying psychological issues contributing to the behavior.",
