                        "cot": " \n\n1. The first thing we need to do is gather more information from the mother. We need to know how often this is happening, what time of day it is happening, and if there are any other unusual behaviors that the mother has noticed. \n\n2. We also need to talk to the patient to get his side of the story. We need to know how he feels about what is happening, and if he is experiencing any other unusual thoughts or behaviors. \n\n3. Based on the information we gather from the mother and the patient, we will need to decide if there is a problem that needs to be addressed. If there is no problem, then we can reassure the mother and tell her that this is normal behavior for a teenage boy. \n\n4. If there is a problem, then we will need to refer the patient for behavioral therapy.",
