                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step. \n\nThe first thing to consider is the patient's age. If the patient were a minor, then the wife would not have the authority to make decisions on his behalf, and a blood transfusion would be administered.\n\nThe next thing to consider is the patient's mental state. If the patient were unconscious or otherwise unable to make decisions for himself, then the wife would be his legal guardian and would be able to make decisions on his behalf. In this case, a blood transfusion would be administered.\n\nThe next thing to consider is the patient's religion. If the patient's religion prohibits blood transfusions, then the patient's wishes should be respected and no blood transfusion should be administered.\n\nThe final thing to consider is the patient's wife. If the patient's wife is opposed to blood transfusions, then the patient's wishes should be respected and no blood transfusion should be administered.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
