                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert.\n\n1) If the patient is of legal age and has capacity, then his wishes should be respected.\n\n2) If the patient is not of legal age or does not have capacity, then a surrogate decision maker should be consulted.\n\n3) If there is no surrogate decision maker, then the decision should be made in the best interests of the patient.\n\nIn this case, the patient is of legal age and has capacity. Therefore, his wishes should be respected and no blood transfusion should be administered.",
