                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Administer a blood transfusion to save the patient's life - This option seems to be the most medically appropriate course of action, but it conflicts with the patient's religious beliefs and written instructions.\n\nB) Call the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue - This option could be helpful in determining the best course of action, but it may take too much time and the patient's life could be at risk.\n\nC) Respect the patient's written instructions and do not administer a blood transfusion - This option respects the patient's autonomy and religious beliefs, but it could result in the patient's death.\n\nD) Convince the wife to administer a blood transfusion to her husband - This option may not be feasible if the wife is strongly opposed to blood transfusions for religious reasons.\n\nE) Refuse to treat the patient as he will die without a blood transfusion - This option is not ethical as it violates the principle of beneficence and could result in the patient's death.\n\nBased on these considerations, the best option is B) Call the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue. This will allow for a thorough discussion of the ethical and medical considerations involved and may lead to a resolution that respects the patient's autonomy while also ensuring that he receives the medical treatment he needs to survive.",
