                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The first step in this situation is to assess the patient's capacity to make decisions about his own medical care. Since the patient is unconscious and unable to communicate his wishes, we must rely on the information provided by his wife and his medical chart.\n\nThe patient's wife has made it clear that he should not receive a blood transfusion under any circumstances, and the medical chart also indicates that the patient has refused blood transfusions for religious reasons. This suggests that the patient has made an informed decision about his medical care and has communicated this decision to his healthcare providers.\n\nGiven this information, the most appropriate course of action is to respect the patient's autonomy and follow his written instructions not to administer a blood transfusion (Option C). While it may be difficult for the healthcare team to accept that the patient may die without a blood transfusion, it is important to respect the patient's right to make decisions about his own medical care, even if those decisions may result in harm or death.\n\nIt is not appropriate to administer a blood transfusion against the patient's wishes (Option A), as this would violate the patient's autonomy and could potentially result in legal and ethical consequences for the healthcare team.\n\nCalling the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue (Option B) may be a helpful step in some situations, but it is unlikely to change the fact that the patient has clearly expressed his wishes not to receive a blood transfusion.\n\nAttempting to convince the wife to change her husband's decision (Option D) is also not appropriate, as it is the patient's autonomy that must be respected, not the wishes of his family members.\n\nRefusing to treat the patient altogether (Option E) is not an acceptable option, as healthcare providers have a duty to provide care to the best of their ability within the constraints of the patient's wishes. In this case, the healthcare team should proceed with the surgery to reattach the patient's arm and provide any other necessary medical care, while respecting the patient's decision not to receive a blood transfusion.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "88485cb6-5ebd-4931-b94d-3298dfcd0884",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Respect the patient's written instructions and do not administer a blood transfusion.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 23:22:48",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-4', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "40a8f9ec-ffb0-4f20-a769-52173b671ae2",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: A 27-year-old man needs emergency surgery to reattach his left arm after a car accident and has lost a lot of blood. His wife and medical chart state that he should not receive blood transfusions for religious reasons. What should you do in this situation?\nA) Give the patient a blood transfusion to save his life\nB) Contact the hospital's ethics board to discuss the issue\nC) Follow the patient's written instructions and do not give a blood transfusion\nD) Persuade the wife to allow a blood transfusion for her husband\nE) Refuse to treat the patient because he will die without a blood transfusion\n\nStep 1: Consider the patient's autonomy and wishes\nThe patient's medical chart and his wife both indicate that he does not want to receive blood transfusions for religious reasons. This suggests that the patient has made a conscious decision not to receive blood transfusions, and his autonomy should be respected.\n\nStep 2: Consider the potential consequences of not administering a blood transfusion\nNot giving the patient a blood transfusion could result in his death. However, administering a blood transfusion against his wishes could also have negative consequences, such as causing emotional distress for the patient and his family, and potentially legal issues for the healthcare provider.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the options\nA) Administering a blood transfusion against the patient's wishes could save his life, but it would violate his autonomy and potentially cause other negative consequences.\nB) Calling the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue could provide guidance on how to proceed in this difficult situation.\nC) Respecting the patient's written instructions and not administering a blood transfusion would honor his autonomy, but it could result in his death.\nD) Convincing the wife to administer a blood transfusion to her husband might not be possible, and it could still go against the patient's wishes.\nE) Refusing to treat the patient would not be an appropriate response, as healthcare providers have a duty to provide care to the best of their ability.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best option\nThe best option in this situation is B) Call the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue. This allows for a discussion of the ethical dilemma and potential guidance on how to proceed while respecting the patient's autonomy and considering the potential consequences of not administering a blood transfusion.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c4d398b1-2041-46d6-97dd-1f6d50344416",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Contact the hospital's ethics board to discuss the issue.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 23:23:55",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-4', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
