                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) Respect the patient's written instructions and do not administer a blood transfusion.\n\nCritique: While it is important to respect the patient's wishes, it is also crucial to consider the potential consequences of not administering a blood transfusion, which could be life-threatening in this case. Additionally, the wife's presence and insistence on not giving a blood transfusion adds another layer of complexity to the situation.\n\nConsidering the other options:\n\nA) Administering a blood transfusion without consent could lead to legal and ethical issues, as it goes against the patient's expressed wishes.\n\nB) Calling the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue could be a reasonable option, as it would allow for a more informed decision to be made, taking into account the patient's wishes, the wife's concerns, and the potential consequences of not administering a blood transfusion.\n\nD) Convincing the wife to administer a blood transfusion to her husband could be a potential option, but it may not be successful, and it could also lead to ethical issues if the patient's wishes are not respected.\n\nE) Refusing to treat the patient is not a viable option, as it would go against the physician's duty to provide care.\n\nFinal answer: B) Call the ethics board of the hospital to discuss the issue.",
