                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question to make sure we understand it correctly: What organism is most likely responsible for this patient's symptoms, and what characteristics does it have?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts & reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nBased on the patient's symptoms and history, the most likely cause of his illness is an infectious agent. The patient has a fever, cough, headache, and diarrhea, and has recently returned from a trip abroad where he was exposed to a variety of potential sources of infection, including kayaking, spas, local animals, and local foods. The chest exam reveals fine crackles on auscultation and the chest radiograph reveals patchy infiltrates in both lungs, which suggests a pulmonary infection. The mild hyponatremia and mild elevation of AST/ALT levels are also consistent with an infectious process.\n\nBased on this information, the organism that is most likely responsible for this patient's symptoms is likely to be a bacteria or virus. Bacteria can form an endospore, while viruses have no cell wall. Bacteria can also have a rabbit reservoir, while viruses are more commonly transmitted by air conditioning.\n\nThird, make sure we have the right answer:\n\nThe organism that is most likely responsible for this patient's symptoms is likely to be a bacteria or virus, and is associated with the characteristics of forming an endospore (A), having a rabbit reservoir (B), having no cell wall (C), and being transmitted by air conditioning (E). It is not associated with being more common in parrot owners (D).",
