                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nA type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is false, yet is accepted in error.\n\nA) A type 1 error means the study is not significantly powered to detect a true difference between study groups. - Incorrect\nB) A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is true but is rejected in error. - Incorrect\nC) A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is false, yet is accepted in error. - Correct\nD) A type 1 error is a beta (\u03b2) error and is usually 0.1 or 0.2. - Incorrect\nE) A type 1 error is dependent on the confidence interval of a study. - Incorrect",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "900110ee-5ed9-4c42-b6e2-238c958b9c46",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
