                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nA type 1 error is when the null hypothesis is false, yet is accepted in error. \n\nThe null hypothesis in this case is that mepolizumab has no effect on reducing asthma exacerbations. \n\nThe alternative hypothesis is that mepolizumab does reduce asthma exacerbations. \n\nSo if the authors had inadvertently encountered a type 1 error, they would have accepted the null hypothesis when it was actually false.",
