                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Analyze the symptoms and identify the illness.\n- Sudden drooping of the right side of the face\n- Drooling and excessive tearing\n- Inability to whistle or close the right eye\n- Circular red rash with central clearing on the trunk\n- Decreased taste sensation\n\nThese symptoms are consistent with Lyme disease, which is caused by the bacterium Borrelia burgdorferi.\n\nStep 2: Identify the vector responsible for transmitting the organism.\nLyme disease is transmitted to humans through the bite of infected black-legged ticks. The options given are:\n\nA) Ixodes scapularis - Black-legged tick\nB) Tsetse fly - Transmits African trypanosomiasis (sleeping sickness)\nC) Culicidae - Mosquito family, transmits various diseases like malaria, dengue, etc.\nD) Dermacentor variabilis - American dog tick, transmits Rocky Mountain spotted fever\nE) Anopheles - Mosquito genus, transmits malaria\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer.\nThe correct answer is A) Ixodes scapularis, as it is the black-legged tick responsible for transmitting Lyme disease.",
