                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe patient has diabetes and hypertension, and was prescribed enalapril and metformin. Enalapril is an ACE inhibitor, while metformin is a biguanide. These two drugs are used to treat hypertension and diabetes, respectively.\n\nThe patient's blood pressure is 155/90 mmHg. This is considered to be stage 2 hypertension, which is defined as a systolic blood pressure of 140-159 mmHg or a diastolic blood pressure of 90-99 mmHg.\n\nThe patient's physician adds another anti-hypertensive medication to the patient's regimen. This could be any number of drugs, but the most likely drug is a diuretic. Diuretics are often used to treat hypertension by reducing the amount of fluid in the body.\n\nThe patient returns to the physician one month later, complaining of new onset lower extremity swelling. This is a common side effect of diuretics. Therefore, the most likely medication that was prescribed to this patient is hydrochlorothiazide, a diuretic.",
