                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient's physician added another anti-hypertensive medication to the patient's regimen, so the answer is not A) Metoprolol.\n\nThe patient is complaining of new onset lower extremity swelling, which could be a symptom of edema, or fluid retention. Therefore, the most likely medication prescribed to this patient is D) Hydrochlorthiazide, which is a diuretic that helps reduce fluid retention.",
