                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes. Dapsone works by inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol, which is a component of the cell membrane of fungi and bacteria. This inhibits the growth of the microorganisms, thus treating the infection. Additionally, dapsone has immunomodulatory effects, which are thought to be due to its ability to inhibit the production of pro-inflammatory cytokines.",
