                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking for the mechanism of action of dapsone in treating bacterial and fungal infections and its immunomodulatory actions.\n\nStep 2: Review the answer choices\nA) Inhibition of cell wall synthesis\nB) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes\nC) Inhibition of protein synthesis\nD) Competition with PABA in folic acid synthesis\n\nStep 3: Recall information about dapsone\nDapsone is a sulfone antibiotic that is primarily used for the treatment of leprosy and other skin infections. It has both antimicrobial and anti-inflammatory properties.\n\nStep 4: Match the mechanism of action with the answer choices\nDapsone works by competing with para-aminobenzoic acid (PABA) for the enzyme dihydropteroate synthase, which is involved in the synthesis of folic acid. By inhibiting this enzyme, dapsone prevents the formation of folic acid, which is essential for the growth and reproduction of bacteria.\n\nStep 5: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) Competition with PABA in folic acid synthesis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "169842cc-4621-454e-8095-d0a81e2f0238",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
