                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes\n\nExplanation: Dapsone works by inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol, a key component of the cell membrane of fungi and bacteria. This prevents the formation of the cell wall, which is essential for the survival of the organisms. It also interferes with the production of folic acid, which is necessary for the growth and reproduction of the organisms.",
