                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion rephrased: What is the mechanism of action of dapsone for bacterial and fungal infections as well as for immunomodulatory actions?\n\nAnswer: B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes.\n\nExplanation: Dapsone is an antimicrobial drug that works by inhibiting the synthesis of ergosterol, a key component of the cell membrane of fungi and bacteria. This inhibition of ergosterol synthesis disrupts the cell membrane, leading to cell death. Additionally, dapsone has immunomodulatory effects, which are thought to be due to its ability to inhibit the production of pro-inflammatory cytokines.",
