                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What is the mechanism of dapsone for its indications?\n\nProfessor: Dapsone works by inhibiting cell wall synthesis. This means that it prevents bacteria from forming a protective wall around themselves, making them more vulnerable to attack by the immune system. It also inhibits ergosterol in cell membranes, which is a type of fat that helps keep the cell membrane intact. Finally, it inhibits protein synthesis, which is necessary for the growth and reproduction of bacteria. So, the mechanism of dapsone for its indications is A) Inhibition of cell wall synthesis, B) Inhibition of ergosterol in cell membranes, and C) Inhibition of protein synthesis.",
                        "answers": [
