                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand what intestinal malabsorption is and the role of each test in assessing it. Intestinal malabsorption is a condition in which the small intestine cannot absorb nutrients properly, leading to various health problems.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n- Intestinal malabsorption can be caused by various factors, such as celiac disease, Crohn's disease, lactose intolerance, and pancreatic insufficiency.\n- Fecal fat estimation measures the amount of fat in the stool, which can indicate malabsorption if the levels are high.\n- Serum lactose levels can help diagnose lactose intolerance, which is a specific type of malabsorption.\n- Serum amylase levels are used to assess pancreatic function, as amylase is an enzyme produced by the pancreas that helps break down carbohydrates.\n- NBT-PABA test (N-benzoyl-L-tyrosyl-p-aminobenzoic acid test) is a test used to assess pancreatic exocrine function, which can be related to malabsorption.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Which test is most comprehensive in assessing intestinal malabsorption?\n2) Which test is most specific to the overall condition of intestinal malabsorption?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1) Fecal fat estimation is the most comprehensive test, as it directly measures the amount of fat in the stool, which can indicate malabsorption if the levels are high.\n2) Fecal fat estimation is also the most specific test for the overall condition of intestinal malabsorption, as it directly measures the end result of the absorption process.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nThe best test for assessment of intestinal malabsorption is A) Fecal fat estimation, as it is the most comprehensive and specific test for the overall condition of intestinal malabsorption.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "738e6bbb-ff19-471c-a13a-f4bd9136f059",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Fecal fat estimation.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
