                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n1. When the muscle is at rest, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is at rest.\n2. When the muscle is contracted, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is contracted.\n3. When the muscle is stretched, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is stretched.\n4. When the muscle is relaxed, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is relaxed.\n5. When the muscle is contracted, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is relaxed.\n6. When the muscle is stretched, the Golgi tendon organ will send a signal to the efferent neuron that the muscle is contracted.\n\nSo, the answer is D.\nGolgi tendon organ continuously relays to the efferent neurons the tension in the muscle.",
