                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the Golgi tendon organ\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a sensory receptor located in the tendons of muscles. It is responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension.\n\nStep 2: Understand voluntary movements\nVoluntary movements are movements that are under conscious control. They involve the activation of efferent neurons, which carry signals from the brain to the muscles.\n\nStep 3: Determine the role of the Golgi tendon organ in voluntary movements\nSince the Golgi tendon organ detects changes in muscle tension, it is important in voluntary movements because it continuously relays information about the tension in the muscle to the efferent neurons. This information is used by the brain to adjust the force of the muscle contraction and ensure that the movement is smooth and controlled.\n\nStep 4: Match the answer to the question\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is D) Tension in the muscle.",
