                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is D) Tension in the muscle.\n\nHere's the reasoning:\n\n1. Golgi tendon organ (GTO) is a sensory receptor located in the tendons of skeletal muscles.\n2. GTO is sensitive to changes in tension or force applied to the muscle.\n3. During voluntary movements, the muscle contracts and generates tension.\n4. The GTO continuously monitors the tension in the muscle and relays this information to the efferent neurons.\n5. Efferent neurons are responsible for carrying signals from the central nervous system to the muscles, causing them to contract or relax.\n6. By relaying information about the tension in the muscle, the GTO helps the efferent neurons to adjust the muscle contraction and maintain the desired level of force or movement.\n7. Therefore, the tension in the muscle is the most important information that the GTO provides during voluntary movements.",
                        "answers": [
