                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to understand what the Golgi tendon organ (GTO) is. The GTO is a sensory receptor located in the tendons of muscles that detects changes in tension or force within the muscle. When the tension in the muscle increases, the GTO sends signals to the spinal cord, which in turn sends signals to the muscle to relax and prevent further tension buildup.\n\nWith this in mind, the answer to the question is D) Tension in the muscle. During voluntary movements, the GTO continuously relays information about the tension in the muscle to the efferent neurons (neurons that carry signals away from the central nervous system to the muscles). This allows the nervous system to regulate the amount of force being produced by the muscle and adjust it as needed to perform the movement accurately and efficiently.",
