                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Golgi tendon organ (GTO) is a proprioceptive sensory receptor organ that is located at the junction of a muscle and its tendon. Its primary function is to monitor the tension within the muscle during voluntary movements.\n\nA) Length of the muscle at rest - This is not the primary function of the GTO, as it is more concerned with muscle tension during movement rather than the resting length of the muscle.\n\nB) Change in angle of joint during motion - This is more related to the function of muscle spindles, which are responsible for detecting changes in muscle length and the rate of change in length.\n\nC) Change in length of muscle before and after the movement - Again, this is more related to the function of muscle spindles, which detect changes in muscle length.\n\nD) Tension in the muscle - This is the primary function of the Golgi tendon organ. It continuously relays information about muscle tension to the efferent neurons, which helps in regulating muscle force and preventing muscle damage due to excessive tension.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Tension in the muscle",
