                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What information does the Golgi tendon organ continuously relay to efferent neurons during voluntary movements?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Voluntary movements involve the contraction and relaxation of muscles.\n- The Golgi tendon organ is a sensory receptor located at the junction of the muscle and tendon.\n- Its main function is to detect changes in muscle tension.\n- When muscle tension increases, the Golgi tendon organ sends signals to the spinal cord via afferent neurons.\n- These signals inhibit the alpha motor neurons that innervate the same muscle, causing it to relax.\n- Therefore, the Golgi tendon organ acts as a protective mechanism against excessive muscle force that could damage the muscle or its attachments.\n- Given this information, the answer is D) Tension in the muscle.\n\nAnswer: D) Tension in the muscle.",
