                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Golgi tendon organ (GTO) is a proprioceptive sensory receptor organ that is located at the junction of muscle fibers and tendons. Its primary function is to monitor and provide feedback on muscle tension during voluntary movements. This information is crucial for maintaining muscle tone, preventing muscle damage, and ensuring smooth and coordinated movements.\n\nTo answer the original question, we need to determine which of the given options best describes the information that the GTO relays to the efferent neurons during voluntary movements.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Does the GTO relay information about the length of the muscle at rest?\n2) Does the GTO relay information about the change in angle of the joint during motion?\n3) Does the GTO relay information about the change in length of the muscle before and after the movement?\n4) Does the GTO relay information about the tension in the muscle?\n\nAnswers to sub-questions:\n1) No, the GTO does not relay information about the length of the muscle at rest. This information is primarily provided by muscle spindles, which are specialized sensory receptors that detect changes in muscle length.\n2) No, the GTO does not relay information about the change in angle of the joint during motion. This information is primarily provided by joint receptors, which are specialized sensory receptors that detect changes in joint position and movement.\n3) No, the GTO does not relay information about the change in length of the muscle before and after the movement. As mentioned earlier, muscle spindles are primarily responsible for detecting changes in muscle length.\n4) Yes, the GTO relays information about the tension in the muscle during voluntary movements. This is the primary function of the GTO, as it helps to maintain muscle tone, prevent muscle damage, and ensure smooth and coordinated movements.\n\nBased on the answers to the sub-questions, the correct answer to the original question is:\n\nD) Tension in the muscle",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "50da9f59-5edf-4bd1-8a6a-8e8ec057d0f9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Tension in the muscle.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
