                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in tendons, which are responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension. They play a crucial role in maintaining muscle tone and preventing muscle damage due to excessive tension.\n\nA) Length of the muscle at rest - This is not the primary function of Golgi tendon organs, as they are more concerned with muscle tension rather than muscle length at rest.\n\nB) Change in angle of joint during motion - This is more related to the function of muscle spindles, which are responsible for detecting changes in muscle length and the rate of change in length.\n\nC) Change in length of muscle before and after the movement - Again, this is more related to the function of muscle spindles, which detect changes in muscle length.\n\nD) Tension in the muscle - This is the primary function of Golgi tendon organs. They continuously relay information about muscle tension to efferent neurons, which helps in regulating muscle contraction and preventing muscle damage due to excessive tension.\n\nSo, the correct answer is D) Tension in the muscle.",
