                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a sensor located at the junction of a muscle and tendon. It monitors the tension in the muscle and relays this information to the efferent neurons. This information is then used to adjust the muscle contraction so that the correct amount of force is generated.\n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is important for voluntary movements because it allows the body to adjust the muscle contraction in response to changes in the tension in the muscle. This ensures that the correct amount of force is generated and that the movement is smooth and coordinated.",
                        "answers": [
