                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) Change in length of muscle before and after the movement.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we must first understand the role of the Golgi tendon organ. The Golgi tendon organ is a sensory receptor located in the tendons of muscles. It is responsible for detecting changes in tension in the muscle and relaying this information to the efferent neurons.\n\nTherefore, the Golgi tendon organ is not responsible for detecting the length of the muscle at rest (A), the change in angle of joint during motion (B), or the tension in the muscle (D). It is only responsible for detecting the change in length of the muscle before and after the movement (C).",
