                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What role does the Golgi tendon organ play during voluntary movements?\n\nProfessor: The Golgi tendon organ plays an important role during voluntary movements by continuously relaying information to the efferent neurons about the length of the muscle at rest, the change in angle of joint during motion, the change in length of muscle before and after the movement, and the tension in the muscle. Does that make sense?\n\nStudent: Yes, that makes sense. So, the Golgi tendon organ is responsible for monitoring the length of the muscle at rest, the change in angle of joint during motion, the change in length of muscle before and after the movement, and the tension in the muscle?\n\nProfessor: That's right. The Golgi tendon organ is responsible for monitoring all of those things during voluntary movements.",
