                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand what resuscitation means in the medical context.\n2. Research the different methods used for managing resuscitation.\n3. Evaluate each option and determine which one is the best guide for managing resuscitation.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Resuscitation refers to the process of reviving a person who has stopped breathing or whose heart has stopped beating.\n2. The different methods used for managing resuscitation include monitoring vital signs such as blood pressure, heart rate, oxygen saturation, and urine output. \n3. Out of the options given, the best guide for the management of resuscitation is D) Saturation of Oxygen. This is because oxygen saturation is a critical indicator of the patient's respiratory status and can help determine if the patient is receiving enough oxygen to support their vital organs. It is also a key parameter used in determining the need for mechanical ventilation or other respiratory support. While the other options may also be important in managing resuscitation, oxygen saturation is the most critical parameter to monitor.",
