                    {
                        "id": "44c7924d-a17f-46bc-b0a4-3f6cc31a2341",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Resuscitation is the process of reviving a person who is in a state of unconsciousness or near-death. It involves restoring breathing and circulation to the body. The management of resuscitation involves monitoring various vital signs to ensure that the person is responding to treatment.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is CVP?\n2. How is urine output related to resuscitation?\n3. Why is blood pressure important in resuscitation?\n4. What is saturation of oxygen and how is it measured?\n\nAnswers:\n1. CVP stands for central venous pressure, which is the pressure in the large veins near the heart. It is used to monitor the fluid status of the body and can be helpful in guiding fluid resuscitation.\n2. Urine output is an important indicator of kidney function and fluid balance. In resuscitation, monitoring urine output can help determine if the body is responding to fluid resuscitation.\n3. Blood pressure is a measure of the force of blood against the walls of the arteries. In resuscitation, maintaining adequate blood pressure is important to ensure that the body's organs are receiving enough oxygen and nutrients.\n4. Saturation of oxygen refers to the amount of oxygen that is bound to hemoglobin in the blood. It is measured using a pulse oximeter, which is a non-invasive device that clips onto a finger or earlobe. Monitoring saturation of oxygen is important in resuscitation to ensure that the person is receiving enough oxygen to support organ function. \n\nAnswer: D) Saturation of Oxygen is the best guide for the management of resuscitation.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3b82b4d1-8bc8-4e9b-9607-2917076416ea",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Saturation of Oxygen.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
