                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking for the best guide for the management of resuscitation.\n\nStep 2: Define resuscitation\nResuscitation is the process of reviving a person who is unconscious, not breathing, or in cardiac arrest.\n\nStep 3: Understand the options\nA) CVP (Central Venous Pressure) - measures the pressure in the large veins near the heart\nB) Urine output - measures the amount of urine produced by the kidneys\nC) Blood pressure - measures the force of blood against the walls of arteries\nD) Saturation of Oxygen - measures the amount of oxygen in the blood\n\nStep 4: Eliminate options\nOption A (CVP) and Option B (Urine output) are not the best guides for the management of resuscitation as they do not directly measure the effectiveness of resuscitation. \n\nStep 5: Choose the best option\nOption C (Blood pressure) is important in resuscitation, but it is not the best guide as it can be affected by many factors and may not accurately reflect the patient's condition. \n\nOption D (Saturation of Oxygen) is the best guide for the management of resuscitation as it directly measures the amount of oxygen in the blood, which is crucial for the patient's survival. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Saturation of Oxygen.",
                        "answers": [
