                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe best guide for the management of Resuscitation is D) Saturation of Oxygen. This is because oxygen saturation is a key indicator of the effectiveness of resuscitation efforts. Oxygen saturation is a measure of the amount of oxygen in the blood, and is typically measured using a pulse oximeter. Low oxygen saturation levels indicate that the patient is not receiving enough oxygen, and that resuscitation efforts should be increased. In contrast, CVP, urine output, and blood pressure are all measures of the patient's overall health, but do not provide direct information about the effectiveness of resuscitation efforts.",
