                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which natural disaster causes the maximum deaths, we need to analyze each option and compare their impact on human life.\n\nA) Hydrological disasters include floods, tsunamis, and hurricanes. These disasters can cause significant damage to infrastructure and homes, leading to displacement and loss of life. However, with proper warning systems and evacuation plans, the death toll can be minimized.\n\nB) Meteorological disasters include tornadoes, cyclones, and blizzards. These disasters can cause significant damage to property and infrastructure, leading to displacement and loss of life. However, with proper warning systems and evacuation plans, the death toll can be minimized.\n\nC) Geological disasters include earthquakes, landslides, and volcanic eruptions. These disasters can cause significant damage to property and infrastructure, leading to displacement and loss of life. Unlike hydrological and meteorological disasters, geological disasters are often sudden and unpredictable, making it difficult to prepare and evacuate people in time. Therefore, the death toll can be higher in these disasters.\n\nD) Fires can be caused by natural or human factors and can cause significant damage to property and infrastructure, leading to displacement and loss of life. However, with proper fire safety measures and evacuation plans, the death toll can be minimized.\n\nBased on the above analysis, it can be concluded that geological disasters (option C) cause the maximum deaths as they are often sudden and unpredictable, making it difficult to prepare and evacuate people in time.",
