                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: What type of natural disaster causes the most deaths?\n\nAnswer: B) Meteorological\n\nExplanation: Meteorological disasters, such as hurricanes, floods, and tornadoes, are the type of natural disasters that cause the most deaths. Hydrological disasters, such as tsunamis, can cause a lot of destruction, but they are not as deadly as meteorological disasters. Geological disasters, such as earthquakes, can cause a lot of destruction, but they are not as deadly as meteorological disasters. Fires, while they can cause a lot of destruction, are not as deadly as meteorological disasters. Therefore, the type of natural disaster that causes the most deaths is meteorological.",
