                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) Antenatal preeclampsia.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we must first understand what is meant by a \"high risk infant.\" A high risk infant is an infant who is at an increased risk of developing health problems due to certain factors.\n\nNext, we must look at each of the options and determine which one is most likely to put an infant at an increased risk of developing health problems.\n\nA) Working mother: A working mother is not necessarily a risk factor for an infant's health. Therefore, this is not the correct answer.\n\nB) Antenatal preeclampsia: Antenatal preeclampsia is a condition that can occur during pregnancy and can put the infant at an increased risk of developing health problems. Therefore, this is the correct answer.\n\nC) Third child: Having a third child is not necessarily a risk factor for an infant's health. Therefore, this is not the correct answer.\n\nD) Twins: Having twins is not necessarily a risk factor for an infant's health. Therefore, this is not the correct answer.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is B) Antenatal preeclampsia.",
