                        "cot": "\nQuestion: Which of the following is considered a high risk infant?\n\nAnswer: B) Antenatal preeclampsia.\n\nExplanation: A high risk infant is defined as an infant who is at an increased risk of developing health problems due to certain factors, such as prematurity, low birth weight, or medical conditions. Antenatal preeclampsia is a medical condition that can cause high blood pressure and other complications during pregnancy, and is therefore considered a high risk infant. Working mother, third child, and twins are not considered high risk infants.",
