                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the research question and the potential factors that may affect the results.\n2. Determine the population from which the sample will be drawn.\n3. Choose a sampling method that will allow for the selection of patients based on the potential factors identified in step 1.\n4. Select the sample using the chosen sampling method.\n\nGoing through each option:\nA) Systematic random sampling: This method involves selecting every nth patient from a list of the population. It does not take into account potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\nB) Simple random sampling: This method involves selecting patients randomly from the population. It also does not take into account potential factors, so it is not the correct answer.\nC) Stratified random sampling: This method involves dividing the population into subgroups based on potential factors and then randomly selecting patients from each subgroup. This is the correct answer as it allows for the selection of patients based on potential factors.\nD) Cluster sampling: This method involves selecting clusters of patients (such as hospitals or clinics) and then randomly selecting patients from within those clusters. It does not necessarily take into account potential factors, so it is not the correct answer. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Stratified random sampling.",
