                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which sampling method is used for selecting patients while considering potential factors that may affect the results.\n\nStep 2: Analyze each option\nA) Systematic random sampling: This method involves selecting every nth individual from a population. It does not take into account any specific factors that may affect the results.\n\nB) Simple random sampling: This method involves selecting individuals randomly from a population without considering any specific factors. It also does not take into account any factors that may affect the results.\n\nC) Stratified random sampling: This method involves dividing the population into subgroups (strata) based on specific factors and then selecting individuals randomly from each subgroup. This method takes into account potential factors that may affect the results.\n\nD) Cluster sampling: This method involves dividing the population into clusters and then selecting entire clusters randomly. It does not specifically consider factors that may affect the results.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is C) Stratified random sampling, as it takes into account potential factors that may affect the results.",
                        "answers": [
