                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Lumbar puncture\n\nLumbar puncture is not routinely done in patients with altered sensorium unless there is a suspicion of meningitis or encephalitis. The other tests, including complete blood counts, random blood sugar, and non-contrast CT head, are commonly done to evaluate the cause of altered sensorium.",
