                        "cot": "\n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education - This statement is true. The HDI only considers gross enrolment in secondary education, not primary education.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy - This statement is true. Adult literacy is one of the three components of the HDI, and it is given a weightage of 1/3rd.\n\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment - This statement is true. Gross enrolment is one of the three components of the HDI, and it is given a weightage of 2/3rd.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy - This statement is false. The HDI takes into account three components - life expectancy, education, and income. Adult literacy is just one aspect of the education component, and the country's achievement is not computed solely on the basis of adult literacy.",
