                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to calculate the Gross Enrolment Ratio. This is the number of people enrolled in school, divided by the number of people of school-going age. \n\nNext, we need to calculate the Adult Literacy Rate. This is the number of people aged 15 and above who can read and write, divided by the total population aged 15 and above. \n\nLastly, we need to calculate the Life Expectancy at Birth. This is the number of years a newborn baby is expected to live, if current mortality patterns are held constant. \n\nNow, we can calculate the HDI. \n\nThe HDI is calculated by taking the average of the three indices (Gross Enrolment Ratio, Adult Literacy Rate, and Life Expectancy at Birth). \n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education\n\nThis is not a true statement. The Gross Enrolment Ratio includes both primary and secondary education. \n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy\n\nThis is not a true statement. The Adult Literacy Rate is not given a weightage. \n\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolmen\n\nThis is not a true statement. The Gross Enrolment Ratio is not given a weightage. \n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy\n\nThis is not a true statement. The country's achievement is computed on the basis of the three indices (Gross Enrolment Ratio, Adult Literacy Rate, and Life Expectancy at Birth).",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "8806e610-f8f9-48d4-8881-21bbe657b9e5",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " D.",
