                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is D) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.\n\nThe Human Development Index (HDI) is a composite measure of three dimensions of human development: living a long and healthy life (measured by life expectancy), being educated (measured by years of schooling), and having a decent standard of living (measured by Gross National Income per capita). \n\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education: This statement is true. The HDI considers the gross enrolment ratio for both primary and secondary education, but only the secondary education ratio is given weightage.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy: This statement is true. Adult literacy rate is one of the indicators used to measure the education dimension of the HDI, and it is given one-third weightage.\n\nC) 2/3`d weightage is given to gross enrolment: This statement is true. The gross enrolment ratio for secondary education is given two-thirds weightage in the education dimension of the HDI.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy: This statement is false. While adult literacy rate is an important indicator used to measure the education dimension of the HDI, it is not the only indicator. The HDI takes into account both years of schooling and adult literacy rate to measure the education dimension. Additionally, the HDI also considers life expectancy and Gross National Income per capita to measure the other two dimensions of human development.",
