                    {
                        "id": "6a175cd5-0be4-4fc4-80a8-89e0bf179569",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following statements about the calculation of the Human Development Index (HDI) is NOT true?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning so anyone can verify them.\n\nThe Human Development Index (HDI) is a composite index that measures a country's average achievements in three basic aspects of human development: health, education, and income. To calculate the education component of the HDI, two indicators are used: adult literacy rate and gross enrollment ratio.\n\nA) In gross enrollment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\nThis statement is incorrect. Gross enrollment ratio considers primary, secondary, and tertiary education. It is the total enrollment in a specific level of education, regardless of age, expressed as a percentage of the eligible official school-age population corresponding to the same level of education in a given school year.\n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy.\nThis statement is true. In the calculation of the education component of the HDI, adult literacy rate is given a weight of 1/3.\n\nC) 2/3rd weightage is given to gross enrollment.\nThis statement is true. In the calculation of the education component of the HDI, gross enrollment ratio is given a weight of 2/3.\n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.\nThis statement is partially true. A country's achievement in education is computed based on both adult literacy rate and gross enrollment ratio, not just adult literacy rate alone.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) In gross enrollment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education, as this statement is not true regarding the calculation of HDI.",
