                    {
                        "id": "36dfd941-7f90-4518-94a7-06c7d785ed20",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe Human Development Index (HDI) is a measure of a country's average achievements in three basic dimensions of human development:\n\n- A long and healthy life: measured by life expectancy at birth.\n- Access to knowledge: measured by the adult literacy rate (with a two-thirds weighting) and the combined primary, secondary, and tertiary gross enrollment ratio (with a one-third weighting).\n- A decent standard of living: measured by gross national income per capita at purchasing power parity in US dollars.\n\nThe HDI can be calculated for any country, regardless of its level of economic development. The HDI was created by the Pakistani economist Mahbub ul Haq and was first published in 1990 by the United Nations Development Programme (UNDP).\n\nBased on the information given, the correct answer is A. In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f412bee7-77e9-4f0d-8943-3acc102d95e8",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " A.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/16 20:54:25",
                        "api_service": "openai",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-002', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "3696d6b9-bf64-404e-abf2-783b54bae1a6",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-17",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Professor, could you help me understand how to calculate HDI?\n\nProfessor: Sure. HDI is calculated by taking into account three factors: life expectancy, adult literacy, and gross enrolment.\n\nStudent: So life expectancy is weighted equally to adult literacy and gross enrolment?\n\nProfessor: No, life expectancy is given the greatest weight. Adult literacy and gross enrolment are each given a weight of one-third.\n\nStudent: And how is gross enrolment calculated?\n\nProfessor: Only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\n\nStudent: I see. So a country's HDI achievement is based on adult literacy and secondary education enrolment.\n\nProfessor: That's right.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "016f0598-1089-43c0-a1bd-a624145bd9f4",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
