                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: A) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education.\n\nExplanation: The Human Development Index (HDI) is a measure of a country's overall achievement in three basic dimensions of human development: health, education, and income. The calculation of HDI takes into account a variety of factors, including life expectancy, adult literacy, gross enrolment in primary, secondary, and tertiary education, and gross national income per capita. Therefore, option A is incorrect, as primary education is considered in the calculation of HDI. The other three options are all true statements regarding the calculation of HDI.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d73d003e-07bd-40bb-a70a-1da886042c45",
