                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to first understand what valproate is and then identify which side effect is gender-specific.\n\nValproate is a medication used to treat epilepsy, bipolar disorder, and to prevent migraines. It has various side effects, some of which are mentioned in the given options.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS) - This is a hormonal disorder that affects women of reproductive age. It is characterized by irregular periods, high levels of androgens (male hormones), and the presence of small cysts in the ovaries. Since this condition affects only women, it is a gender-specific side effect.\n\nB) Alopecia - This refers to hair loss, which can affect both men and women. Therefore, it is not a gender-specific side effect.\n\nC) Weight loss - This can also affect both men and women, so it is not a gender-specific side effect.\n\nD) Tremor - This is an involuntary shaking movement that can affect both men and women, so it is not a gender-specific side effect.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nA) Polycystic ovarian syndrome, as it is a gender-specific side effect of valproate that affects only women.",
