                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is A) Polycystic ovarian syndrome.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to consider the definition of valproate and the definition of each of the four options. Valproate is an anticonvulsant drug used to treat epilepsy, bipolar disorder, and migraine headaches. It is also sometimes used to treat depression.\n\nPolycystic ovarian syndrome (A) is a condition that affects women and is characterized by an imbalance of hormones, which can lead to irregular menstrual cycles, infertility, and other symptoms. Alopecia (B) is a condition that causes hair loss, but it is not gender-specific. Weight loss (C) is not a gender-specific side-effect of valproate. Tremor (D) is a type of involuntary shaking, but it is not gender-specific.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Polycystic ovarian syndrome, as it is a gender-specific side-effect of valproate.",
