                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nThe first step is to decide what type of data you have. In this case, you have two groups, so you need to compare the means of those groups. This is a comparison of means, so you would use a t-test.\n\nThe second step is to decide what type of t-test you need. In this case, you are comparing the means of two groups, so you would use a two-sample t-test.\n\nThe third step is to decide what your null and alternative hypotheses are. In this case, your null hypothesis would be that the two groups have the same mean. Your alternative hypothesis would be that the two groups have different means.\n\nThe fourth step is to calculate the t-statistic and p-value. The t-statistic is used to determine whether or not the null hypothesis can be rejected. The p-value is used to determine the significance of the results.\n\nThe fifth and final step is to interpret the results. In this case, if the p-value is less than 0.05, you would reject the null hypothesis and conclude that the two groups have different means.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "437f6c9c-767a-4ea4-876b-02e2f6c92612",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " D.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
