                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is B) To determine outliers.\n\nHere's why:\n\nThe statistical Q test is a non-parametric test used to identify outliers in a data set. It is based on the principle that outliers will have a disproportionate effect on the range of the data set. The test involves ranking the data set in ascending order and then calculating the difference between each observation and its corresponding rank. The sum of these differences is then compared to a critical value, which is determined based on the size of the data set and the desired level of significance.\n\nOption A) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups is not correct because the Q test is not used for comparing means of two groups. Instead, t-test or ANOVA is used for this purpose.\n\nOption C) To determine normality distribution is not correct because the Q test is not used to determine normality distribution. Instead, tests like the Shapiro-Wilk test or the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test are used for this purpose.\n\nOption D) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups is not correct because the Q test is not used for comparing means of more than two groups. Instead, ANOVA or Kruskal-Wallis test is used for this purpose.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "8ab478e2-7a38-4c61-af63-871f3743868c",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) To determine outliers.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
