                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Read the question and options carefully.\n\nStep 2: Understand the concept of statistical Q test.\n\nStep 3: Analyze each option and eliminate the ones that are not relevant.\n\nStep 4: Choose the option that best describes the use of statistical Q test.\n\nStep 5: Verify the answer to ensure it is correct.\n\nStep 6: Provide the final answer.\n\nStep 2: Statistical Q test is a non-parametric test used to identify outliers in a dataset.\n\nStep 3: Option A is incorrect because the statistical Q test is not used to compare the proportion of means of two groups. Option C is incorrect because the statistical Q test is not used to determine normality distribution. Option D is incorrect because the statistical Q test is not used to compare the proportion of means of more than two groups.\n\nStep 4: Option B is the correct answer because the statistical Q test is used to determine outliers in a dataset.\n\nStep 5: To verify the answer, we can check the definition of statistical Q test in any statistical textbook or online resource.\n\nStep 6: The correct answer is B) To determine outliers.",
