                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question and the options provided.\n\nThe question is asking about the use of the statistical Q test. The options provided are:\n\nA) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups\nB) To determine outliers\nC) To determine normality distribution\nD) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups\n\nStep 2: Understand the purpose of the Q test.\n\nThe Q test is a statistical test used to determine the presence of outliers in a data set. It is used to identify data points that are significantly different from the rest of the data.\n\nStep 3: Compare the options provided with the purpose of the Q test.\n\nOption A is incorrect because the Q test is not used to compare the proportion of means of 2 groups. This is typically done using a t-test or ANOVA.\n\nOption B is correct because the Q test is used to determine outliers in a data set.\n\nOption C is incorrect because the Q test is not used to determine normality distribution. This is typically done using a normality test such as the Shapiro-Wilk test.\n\nOption D is incorrect because the Q test is not used to compare the proportion of means of more than 2 groups. This is typically done using ANOVA or a similar test.\n\nStep 4: Select the correct answer.\n\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is B) To determine outliers.",
