                        "instruction": "zhou-01-ins",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the options given.\n\nA) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups - This option suggests that the Q test is used to compare the means of two different groups.\n\nB) To determine outliers - This option suggests that the Q test is used to identify data points that are significantly different from the rest of the data.\n\nC) To determine normality distribution - This option suggests that the Q test is used to check if the data follows a normal distribution.\n\nD) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups - This option suggests that the Q test is used to compare the means of multiple groups.\n\nStep 2: Recall the purpose of the Q test.\n\nThe Q test, also known as the Dixon's Q test, is a statistical test used to identify and reject outliers in a data set.\n\nStep 3: Match the purpose of the Q test with the given options.\n\nThe correct option is B) To determine outliers, as the Q test is specifically designed to identify and reject outliers in a data set.",
