                    {
                        "id": "0d2431e2-9153-45d3-8ca5-f96b36b146f3",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question and the given options.\nThe question asks about the purpose of the statistical Q test. The options provided are:\nA) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups\nB) To determine outliers\nC) To determine normality distribution\nD) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups\n\nStep 2: Recall the definition and purpose of the statistical Q test.\nThe Q test, also known as the Dixon's Q test, is a statistical test used to identify and reject outliers in a data set. It is particularly useful when dealing with small sample sizes.\n\nStep 3: Match the purpose of the Q test with the given options.\nBased on the definition and purpose of the Q test, it is clear that the test is used to determine outliers in a data set.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct option.\nThe correct option is B) To determine outliers.",
                        "answers": [
