                    },
                    {
                        "id": "c9353fd0-fbff-408b-9f95-d14db8d26d91",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: What is the purpose of the statistical Q test?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nA) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups - This option suggests that the Q test is used to compare the means of two groups. However, the Q test is not typically used for this purpose. Instead, tests like the t-test or Mann-Whitney U test are used for comparing means of two groups.\n\nB) To determine outliers - The Q test is indeed used to identify potential outliers in a data set. It compares the difference between a suspected outlier and its two neighboring data points to the overall range of the data. If the calculated Q value is greater than a critical Q value (based on the sample size and desired confidence level), the data point is considered an outlier.\n\nC) To determine normality distribution - This option suggests that the Q test is used to determine if a data set follows a normal distribution. However, the Q test is not used for this purpose. Instead, tests like the Shapiro-Wilk test or Kolmogorov-Smirnov test are used to assess normality.\n\nD) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups - This option suggests that the Q test is used to compare the means of multiple groups. However, the Q test is not typically used for this purpose. Instead, tests like ANOVA or Kruskal-Wallis H test are used for comparing means of more than two groups.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nB) To determine outliers",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "aadff2a0-79e8-4a55-930b-b9245f0d6c15",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) To determine outliers.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/14 17:47:24",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-4', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
