                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nThe first thing we need to do is identify the null and alternative hypotheses for this question. The null hypothesis would be that there is no difference in the proportion of means of the two groups, while the alternative hypothesis would be that there is a difference.\n\nNext, we need to calculate a test statistic. For this, we will use the t-statistic.\n\nFinally, we need to compare the t-statistic to a critical value. If the t-statistic is greater than the critical value, we will reject the null hypothesis.",
