                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Comparing the proportion of means of 2 groups - This is typically done using a t-test or a z-test, not a Q test.\n\nB) To determine outliers - The Q test is used to identify potential outliers in a data set, especially in small sample sizes.\n\nC) To determine normality distribution - Normality tests, such as the Shapiro-Wilk test or the Kolmogorov-Smirnov test, are used to determine if a data set follows a normal distribution, not the Q test.\n\nD) Comparing the proportion of means of more than 2 groups - This is typically done using an ANOVA test, not a Q test.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\nB) To determine outliers",
