                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following factors does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis, a severe and potentially life-threatening side effect of Metformin?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step, spelling out our thoughts and reasoning:\n\nA) Advanced age: Older individuals may have decreased kidney function, which can increase the risk of lactic acidosis due to the reduced ability to clear Metformin from the body.\n\nB) Smoking: Smoking can cause various health issues, but it is not directly linked to an increased risk of lactic acidosis in relation to Metformin use.\n\nC) Liver dysfunction: The liver plays a role in clearing lactate from the body. If the liver is not functioning properly, it may not be able to clear lactate effectively, increasing the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nD) Renal failure: Kidney function is crucial for clearing Metformin from the body. If the kidneys are not functioning properly, Metformin can accumulate in the body, increasing the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is B) Smoking, as it is not directly linked to an increased risk of lactic acidosis in relation to Metformin use.",
