                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we'll look at the definition of lactic acidosis: \n\nLactic acidosis is a condition in which there is too much lactic acid in the body. Lactic acid is a waste product that is produced when the body breaks down glucose for energy.\n\nNext, we'll look at the risk factors for lactic acidosis: \n\nThe risk factors for lactic acidosis include:\n\n-Advanced age\n-Smoking\n-Liver dysfunction\n-Renal failure\n\nNow, we'll look at the question again and see which answer choice best fits with the information we have. \n\nThe answer choice that best fits with the information we have is D) Renal failure.",
                        "answers": [
