                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Advanced age - Older people may have a higher risk of lactic acidosis due to decreased kidney function and other age-related factors.\nC) Liver dysfunction - The liver plays a role in clearing lactate from the body, so liver dysfunction can increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\nD) Renal failure - The kidneys also help clear lactate from the body, so renal failure can increase the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nB) Smoking - While smoking is a risk factor for many health issues, it is not directly linked to an increased risk of lactic acidosis in the context of metformin use.\n\nAnswer: B) Smoking",
