                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is B) Smoking.\n\nTo determine this, we must first understand what lactic acidosis is and what causes it. Lactic acidosis is a condition in which there is an accumulation of lactic acid in the body, which can lead to serious health complications. It is caused by an imbalance between the production and removal of lactic acid from the body.\n\nMetformin is a medication used to treat type 2 diabetes. It can cause a severe and sometimes life-threatening side effect of lactic acidosis. The risk of lactic acidosis is increased by certain factors, such as advanced age, liver dysfunction, and renal failure.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) Smoking, as smoking does not increase the risk of lactic acidosis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "960874ee-5641-4ff1-a149-775cd9a33ade",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
