                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Phosphoenol pyruvate carboxykinase: This enzyme is involved in gluconeogenesis, the process of producing glucose from non-carbohydrate sources. It is not directly related to the metabolism of raw eggs.\n\nB) Pyruvate carboxylase: This enzyme is involved in the conversion of pyruvate to oxaloacetate, which is then used in gluconeogenesis. It is not directly related to the metabolism of raw eggs.\n\nC) Glycogen phosphorylase: This enzyme is involved in the breakdown of glycogen to glucose. It is not directly related to the metabolism of raw eggs.\n\nD) Glucose 6 phosphatase: This enzyme is involved in the final step of gluconeogenesis and glycogenolysis, the conversion of glucose-6-phosphate to glucose. It is also involved in the release of glucose from the liver into the bloodstream. A deficiency in this enzyme can cause hypoglycemia, which is consistent with the symptoms presented by the patient.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Glucose 6 phosphatase.",
