                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nAnswer: D) Glucose 6 phosphatase\n\nReasoning: Raw eggs contain avidin, a protein that binds to biotin, a vitamin necessary for the function of enzymes involved in gluconeogenesis (the process of making glucose from non-carbohydrate sources). Without biotin, the enzyme glucose 6 phosphatase cannot function properly, leading to hypoglycemia. The other enzymes listed (phosphoenol pyruvate carboxykinase, pyruvate carboxylase, and glycogen phosphorylase) are not directly involved in gluconeogenesis or affected by biotin deficiency.",
