                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the context of the question\nThe question is asking what should be done after 10 years when an IOL (intraocular lens) has been placed in a young male.\n\nStep 2: Consider the lifespan of an IOL\nIOLs are designed to be a permanent replacement for the natural lens of the eye. They are made of materials that are meant to last a lifetime.\n\nStep 3: Consider potential complications\nOne potential complication that can occur after an IOL is placed is posterior capsule ossification. This is when the capsule that holds the IOL in place becomes thickened and calcified, which can cause vision problems. In this case, the IOL may need to be removed.\n\nStep 4: Consider the age of the patient\nThe question specifies that the patient is a young male. This means that he may not yet have developed presbyopia, which is the natural age-related decline in near vision. Therefore, removing the IOL when presbyopia sets in (option C) may not be relevant.\n\nStep 5: Evaluate the answer options\nOption A suggests that the IOL should be removed in case of posterior capsule ossification, which is a potential complication. This is a valid option to consider.\nOption B suggests that the IOL should never be removed. However, this is not necessarily true as complications can arise that may require removal.\nOption C suggests that the IOL should be removed when presbyopia sets in, but as mentioned earlier, this may not be relevant for a young male.\nOption D suggests that the IOL should be changed after 10 years, but there is no specific reason given for why this would be necessary.\n\nStep 6: Choose the best answer\nBased on the information provided, option A is the most appropriate answer. If posterior capsule ossification occurs, the IOL may need to be removed to prevent vision problems.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d076444e-d7c2-49c1-b7a8-236f6efa02b4",
