                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nAfter 10 years, the IOL may still be functioning well and providing clear vision. However, it is possible that the patient may develop presbyopia, which is a natural age-related condition that affects near vision. In this case, the IOL may need to be replaced with a multifocal or accommodating IOL to address the presbyopia. Additionally, if there is any complication such as posterior capsule ossification, the IOL may need to be removed or exchanged. Therefore, the correct answer is D) Should be changed after 10 years, depending on the patient's individual needs and any complications that may arise.",
