                        "cot": " \n\nStep 1: An IOL is an intraocular lens, which is a type of lens that is surgically implanted in the eye to replace the natural lens. \n\nStep 2: In this case, the IOL was placed in a young male. \n\nStep 3: After 10 years, the IOL should be checked for any signs of Posterior Capsule ossification. If there are any signs, the IOL should be removed. \n\nAnswer: A) IOL should be removed in case of Posterior Capsule ossification",
