                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nQ: IOL placed in the young male., After 10 year what should be done..?\n\nA) IOL should be removed in case of Posterior Capsule ossification\nB) Never be removed\nC) Remove when presbyopia sets in\nD) Should be changed after 10 year\n\nLet's rephrase the question to be sure we understood it correctly:\n\nWhat should be done with an IOL placed in a young male after 10 years?\n\nA) IOL should be removed in case of Posterior Capsule ossification\nB) Never be removed\nC) Remove when presbyopia sets in\nD) Should be changed after 10 year\n\nOur thoughts & reasoning:\n\nOption A) doesn't make sense, because the IOL would only need to be removed if there was ossification of the posterior capsule, and that would likely happen much sooner than 10 years.\n\nOption B) also doesn't make sense, because the IOL would never need to be removed.\n\nOption C) could be correct, because the IOL might need to be removed when presbyopia sets in (around age 40-45).\n\nOption D) could also be correct, because the IOL might need to be changed after 10 years.\n\nThe correct answer is probably either C) or D), but we would need more information to be sure.",
                        "answers": [
