                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: C) Remove when presbyopia sets in.\n\nExplanation: Intraocular lenses (IOLs) are typically placed in young males to correct vision problems. After 10 years, the IOL should be removed when presbyopia sets in, which is the age-related loss of near vision. Removing the IOL at this point can help restore near vision. In cases of posterior capsule ossification, the IOL should be removed, but this is not necessarily the case after 10 years.",
