                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the question.\n\nThe question is asking what should be done with an IOL (intraocular lens) that was placed in a young male 10 years ago.\n\nStep 2: Consider the answer choices.\n\nA) Remove in case of posterior capsule ossification\nB) Never be removed\nC) Remove when presbyopia sets in\nD) Should be changed after 10 years\n\nStep 3: Consider the context.\n\nThe IOL was placed in a young male 10 years ago. This means that the patient is likely not experiencing presbyopia yet, and is unlikely to have posterior capsule ossification.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best answer.\n\nGiven the context, the best answer is B) Never be removed.",
