                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: What is the process by which the amount of a drug in the body decreases after administration, but before entering the systemic circulation called?\n\nAnswer: B) First pass effect\n\nExplanation: The first pass effect is the process by which a drug is metabolized by the liver before entering the systemic circulation. This process reduces the amount of the drug in the body before it reaches the systemic circulation. Excretion is the process by which a drug is eliminated from the body, while first order elimination is a type of pharmacokinetic process that describes the rate at which a drug is eliminated from the body. Metabolism is the process by which a drug is broken down into its metabolites.",
                        "answers": [
