                        "cot": "\nB) First pass effect\n\nThe first pass effect is the process by which a drug is metabolized by the liver before entering the systemic circulation. This process reduces the amount of the drug that is available for systemic circulation, and thus reduces the drug's effectiveness. Excretion is the process by which a drug is eliminated from the body, while metabolism is the process by which a drug is broken down into smaller molecules. First order elimination is a type of drug elimination that follows a predictable pattern.",
