                        "cot": "C) 2-6 years.\n\nCritique: Piaget's theory of cognitive development identifies four stages of development, and the preoperational stage is the second stage. This stage typically occurs between the ages of 2 and 7 years old, so option C is the correct answer. Option A is incorrect because it only covers the first year and a half of life, which is part of the sensorimotor stage. Option B is incorrect because it covers a much broader age range that includes the concrete operational and formal operational stages. Option D is incorrect because it only covers the latter part of the concrete operational stage.\n\nFinal answer: C) 2-6 years.",
