                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what cataract extraction surgery under PCB means?\n\nProfessor: Sure, PCB stands for posterior chamber intraocular lens implantation. It's a type of cataract surgery where the cloudy lens is removed and replaced with an artificial lens implant in the posterior chamber of the eye.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what does post-operative vision effects mean?\n\nProfessor: Post-operative vision effects refer to any changes in vision that occur after the surgery. This could include improvements in vision due to the removal of the cataract, or any complications that may arise from the surgery.\n\nStudent: And what is surveillance in this context?\n\nProfessor: Surveillance refers to the monitoring of patients after the surgery to assess their vision and any potential complications.\n\nStudent: So, which of the options is used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is D) Routine checkup of all operated cases. After the surgery, patients will have regular checkups with their ophthalmologist to monitor their vision and ensure that there are no complications. This is the most effective way to evaluate post-operative vision effects. \n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that to me.",
