                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking for the method used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB (presumably, phacoemulsification with intraocular lens implantation).\n\nStep 2: Define the terms\n- Active surveillance: A system where health officials actively seek out and collect information about cases of a specific disease or condition.\n- Sentinel surveillance: A system where a limited number of selected sites or populations are monitored for a specific disease or condition, often used when active surveillance is not feasible.\n- Passive surveillance: A system where health officials rely on reports of cases from healthcare providers, without actively seeking out information.\n- Routine checkup of all operated cases: A system where all patients who have undergone the surgery are checked regularly for any post-operative complications or effects.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most appropriate method\nIn the context of evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery, it is important to monitor all patients who have undergone the surgery to ensure that any complications or effects are detected and addressed promptly. Therefore, the most appropriate method would be a routine checkup of all operated cases.\n\nAnswer: D) Routine checkup of all operated cases",
