                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding this question about evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB. Can you help me work through it?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's start by understanding what PCB stands for. It's an abbreviation for \"phacoemulsification with intraocular lens implantation under peribulbar anesthesia.\" Now, let's look at the options given and understand what each of them means. \n\nStudent: Okay, let's start with option A, active surveillance.\n\nProfessor: Active surveillance is a method where health professionals actively seek out and collect data on a specific health issue or population. In this case, it would involve actively monitoring patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStudent: What about option B, sentinel surveillance?\n\nProfessor: Sentinel surveillance is a type of surveillance where a limited number of selected sites or populations are monitored, usually because they are considered high-risk or representative of a larger population. In this context, it would involve monitoring a select group of patients who have had the surgery.\n\nStudent: And option C, passive surveillance?\n\nProfessor: Passive surveillance is when data is collected and reported by healthcare providers without any active effort to seek out cases. In this case, it would involve collecting data on post-operative vision effects as patients come in for follow-up appointments or report issues on their own.\n\nStudent: Lastly, option D, routine checkup of all operated cases?\n\nProfessor: This option refers to regularly scheduled follow-up appointments for all patients who have undergone the surgery, regardless of whether they are experiencing any issues or not.\n\nStudent: Based on these definitions, I think the correct answer would be D) Routine checkup of all operated cases, as it would involve evaluating the post-operative vision effects for all patients who have had the surgery. Is that correct?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct! Routine checkup of all operated cases would be the most appropriate method for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB. It ensures that all patients are monitored, and any issues can be detected and addressed promptly. Well done!",
