                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe question is asking which of the following is used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nA) Active surveillance would involve proactively seeking out patients to check on their vision effects post-cataract surgery.\nB) Sentinel surveillance would involve tracking a group of patients over time to see if there are any vision effects post-cataract surgery.\nC) Passive surveillance would involve waiting for patients to come to you with any vision effects post-cataract surgery.\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases would involve checking in with all patients who have had cataract surgery at regular intervals to see if there are any vision effects.\n\nThe answer is D) Routine checkup of all operated cases.",
