                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the question.\nThe question is asking which of the following is used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStep 2: Read the answer choices.\nA) Active surveillance\nB) Sentinel surveillance\nC) Passive surveillance\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the answer choices.\nA) Active surveillance - This is not the correct answer because active surveillance involves actively monitoring a population for a disease or condition.\nB) Sentinel surveillance - This is the correct answer because sentinel surveillance involves monitoring a population for a specific disease or condition by collecting data from a limited number of sites.\nC) Passive surveillance - This is not the correct answer because passive surveillance involves collecting data from existing sources, such as medical records or reports from health care providers.\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases - This is not the correct answer because this is not a form of surveillance.\n\nAnswer: B) Sentinel surveillance",
                        "answers": [
                            {
