                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) Passive surveillance.\n\nTo evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB, passive surveillance is used. Passive surveillance is a type of monitoring system that does not require active participation from the patient or healthcare provider. Instead, it relies on the collection of data from existing sources, such as medical records, laboratory tests, and surveys. In the case of post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery, passive surveillance would involve collecting data from medical records and laboratory tests to assess the patient's vision after the surgery. This data can then be used to evaluate the effectiveness of the surgery and any potential side effects.",
                        "answers": [
