                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: C) Passive surveillance\n\nExplanation: Post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB are typically evaluated using passive surveillance. This means that the patient's vision is monitored over time, but no active intervention is taken unless the patient's vision deteriorates. Active surveillance involves actively monitoring the patient's vision, while sentinel surveillance involves monitoring a sample of patients to detect any changes in vision. Routine checkup of all operated cases is not typically used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.",
