                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nC) Passive surveillance\n\nPassive surveillance is the most commonly used method to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB. This method involves collecting data from patients who have already undergone the surgery and are being monitored for any vision-related issues. This data is then used to assess the effectiveness of the surgery and identify any potential complications. Active surveillance and sentinel surveillance are also used to evaluate post-operative vision effects, but passive surveillance is the most commonly used method. Routine checkup of all operated cases is not used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.",
