                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStudent: What is the best way to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB?\n\nProfessor: To evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB, the best option is C) Passive surveillance. Passive surveillance involves monitoring the patient's vision without actively intervening. This allows us to observe any changes in vision over time. \n\nStudent: What is the difference between passive surveillance and active surveillance?\n\nProfessor: Active surveillance involves actively intervening in the patient's vision, such as providing treatments or medications. Passive surveillance, on the other hand, involves monitoring the patient's vision without actively intervening. This allows us to observe any changes in vision over time.",
