                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Answer: D) Routine checkup of all operated cases\n\nCritique: The answer seems reasonable as it involves checking all the patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery under PCB to evaluate their post-operative vision effects. However, it might be helpful to reconsider the other options to ensure that this is the best choice.\n\nA) Active surveillance: This involves actively searching for cases of a specific condition or disease, which may not be the most efficient way to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nB) Sentinel surveillance: This involves monitoring a select group of patients or locations to detect trends in a specific condition or disease. While this may provide some information on post-operative vision effects, it may not be as comprehensive as checking all operated cases.\n\nC) Passive surveillance: This involves collecting data on cases of a specific condition or disease as they are reported by healthcare providers. This may not be the most effective way to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB, as it relies on healthcare providers to report the information.\n\nFinal answer: D) Routine checkup of all operated cases. This option is the most comprehensive and efficient way to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.",
