                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "D) Routine checkup of all operated cases\n\nCritique: Active surveillance involves actively seeking out cases and collecting data, which is not necessary for routine post-operative checkups. Sentinel surveillance involves monitoring a specific group of patients who are at higher risk for complications, which is not necessary for routine cataract extraction surgery. Passive surveillance involves relying on patients or healthcare providers to report any adverse events, which may not be reliable for detecting subtle changes in vision. Therefore, routine checkups of all operated cases is the most appropriate option for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nFinal answer: D) Routine checkup of all operated cases.",
                        "answers": [
