                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Calculate the change in intrapleural pressure during inspiration: -9 cmH2O - (-4 cmH2O) = -5 cmH2O\n2. Convert the change in pressure to cmH2O/L: -5 cmH2O / 0.5 L = -10 cmH2O/L\n3. Take the absolute value of the result: 10 cmH2O/L\n4. Divide the tidal volume by the absolute change in pressure: 500 mL / 10 cmH2O/L = 0.05 L/cmH2O\n5. Convert the result to L/cm: 0.05 L/cmH2O x 10 cmH2O/L = 0.5 L/cm\n\nAnswer: C) 0.2 L/cm",
