                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe first step is to calculate the change in volume of the lungs, which is 500 mL. The next step is to calculate the change in pressure of the lungs, which is -4 cm of water before inspiration and -9 cm of water after inspiration. This gives a difference in pressure of 5 cm of water. The last step is to divide the change in volume by the change in pressure, which gives a pulmonary compliance of 0.1 L/cm.",
