                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe answer is D.\nThe reasoning is The intrapleural pressure was measured as - 4 cm of water before inspiration and - 9 cm of water after inspiration. The difference between the two measurements is 9 - 4 = 5 cm of water. The tidal volume was 500 mL, so the compliance is 5 cm / 500 mL = 0.1 L/cm.\nThe answer is A.",
