                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Polypoidal choroidal vasculopathy (PCV) is a type of choroidal neovascularization that is associated with age-related macular degeneration (AMD). It is characterized by the presence of abnormal blood vessels that grow into the eye from the choroid, which is the layer of blood vessels beneath the retina. These blood vessels are called polypoidal vessels because they have a distinctive appearance that resembles a polyp, or small growth.\nThe correct answer is D.",
