                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question: What is the name of the test in which the examiner places one hand under the patient's heel and asks the patient to raise their other leg against downward resistance, used to assess lower limb weakness?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step:\n\n1. We are looking for a test that involves placing a hand under the patient's heel and asking them to raise their other leg against resistance.\n2. This test is used to evaluate lower limb weakness in patients.\n\nLet's analyze each option:\n\nA) Hoover test: This test is used to assess the presence of non-organic or functional weakness in the lower limbs. The examiner places one hand under the patient's heel and asks the patient to raise their other leg against resistance. If the patient genuinely tries to lift their leg, the examiner should feel pressure on their hand under the heel. This matches the description given in the question.\n\nB) Waddell's test: This is a group of tests used to identify non-organic or psychogenic components of chronic low back pain. It does not involve placing a hand under the patient's heel and asking them to raise their other leg against resistance.\n\nC) O'Donoghue test: This test is used to evaluate joint injuries, particularly in the knee. It involves passive and active movements of the joint to assess pain and stability. It does not involve placing a hand under the patient's heel and asking them to raise their other leg against resistance.\n\nD) McBride test: This test is used to assess patellar tracking and alignment in patients with patellofemoral pain syndrome. It involves placing the patient's foot on the examiner's knee and applying pressure to the patella while the patient contracts their quadriceps muscle. It does not involve placing a hand under the patient's heel and asking them to raise their other leg against resistance.\n\nBased on our analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nA) Hoover test",
