thyroidism is a possible diagnosis for this child?\n\nStudent: No, the symptoms don't seem to match.\n\nProfessor: Correct. Finally, let's look at Proteus syndrome. What are the main symptoms of this condition?\n\nStudent: Proteus syndrome is a rare genetic disorder that causes overgrowth of various tissues in the body. The main symptoms include asymmetrical overgrowth, skin abnormalities, and an increased risk of developing tumors.\n\n",
