                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what staphylococcus food poisoning is. \n\nAccording to the Mayo Clinic, staphylococcus food poisoning is a type of food poisoning caused by the bacteria staphylococcus. This bacteria is found in the nose and on the skin of humans and animals. It can contaminate food if it comes into contact with it.\n\nThe symptoms of staphylococcus food poisoning include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and abdominal cramps. These symptoms usually occur within 1-6 hours after eating contaminated food.\n\nThe optimum temperature for toxin production is 370C.\n\nThe toxin can be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes.\n\nThe incubation period is 1-6 hours.",
