                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQuestion: What is the characteristic feature of staphylococcus food poisoning that is not true?\n\nStep 1: Staphylococcus food poisoning is caused by toxins produced by the bacteria. These toxins are responsible for the symptoms of food poisoning, such as nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\n\nStep 2: The characteristic features of staphylococcus food poisoning include an optimum temperature for toxin production of 370C, intradietic toxins responsible for intestinal symptoms, and a short incubation period of 1-6 hours.\n\nStep 3: The characteristic feature of staphylococcus food poisoning that is not true is that toxin can be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes. This is not true because boiling does not destroy the toxins produced by staphylococcus bacteria. The correct answer is C) Toxin can be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes.",
