                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) Optimum temperature for toxin production is 370C\n\nStaphylococcus food poisoning is caused by the ingestion of food contaminated with Staphylococcus aureus bacteria. The bacteria produce toxins that cause food poisoning. The optimum temperature for toxin production is 370C, which is higher than the temperature of the human body.\n\nB) Intradietic toxin are responsible for intestinal symptoms\n\nIntradietic toxins are not responsible for intestinal symptoms associated with Staphylococcus food poisoning. Instead, the toxins produced by the bacteria are responsible for the symptoms. These toxins are heat-stable and can survive temperatures up to 370C.\n\nC) Toxin can be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes\n\nToxins produced by Staphylococcus aureus can be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes. This is because the toxins are heat-stable and can survive temperatures up to 370C.\n\nD) Incubation period is 1-6 hours\n\nThe incubation period for Staphylococcus food poisoning is typically 1-6 hours. This is the time between ingestion of the contaminated food and the onset of symptoms. Symptoms typically include nausea, vomiting, abdominal cramps, and diarrhea.\n\nThe characteristic feature of staphylococcus food poisoning that is not true is A) Optimum temperature for toxin production is 370C.",
