                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) DNA repair can occur in both directions as it involves the removal and replacement of damaged nucleotides.\nB) DNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction as new nucleotides are added to the 3' end of the growing strand.\nC) RNA editing can occur in both directions as it involves the modification of RNA molecules after transcription.\nD) Transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction as RNA polymerase reads the template DNA strand in this direction.\n\nTherefore, the answer is none of the above. All of these processes can occur in the 5' to 3' direction except for none of them.",
