                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain the question again, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The question is asking which of the following processes does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStudent: What does 5' to 3' direction mean?\n\nProfessor: The 5' to 3' direction refers to the direction in which DNA or RNA is synthesized. It means that the nucleotides are added to the 3' end of the growing strand.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. So, which of the processes listed doesn't occur in this direction?\n\nProfessor: That would be option C, RNA editing.\n\nStudent: Can you explain why RNA editing doesn't occur in the 5' to 3' direction?\n\nProfessor: RNA editing involves changing the sequence of nucleotides in an RNA molecule after it has been transcribed from DNA. This can happen at various positions along the RNA molecule, so it doesn't necessarily occur in a specific direction.\n\nStudent: I see. And what about the other options?\n\nProfessor: DNA repair, DNA replication, and transcription all occur in the 5' to 3' direction. During DNA replication, for example, the new nucleotides are added to the 3' end of the growing strand. Similarly, during transcription, the RNA molecule is synthesized in the 5' to 3' direction. And during DNA repair, the damaged nucleotides are removed and replaced in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that. It makes sense now.",
                        "answers": [
