                    },
                    {
                        "id": "eb3db081-dbe3-4c88-8963-7ce6c046c6d5",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: Which of the following processes does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step, spelling out our thoughts and reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nA) DNA repair: DNA repair mechanisms, such as base excision repair and nucleotide excision repair, involve the synthesis of new DNA strands in the 5' to 3' direction. So, DNA repair occurs in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nB) DNA replication: During DNA replication, the new DNA strand is synthesized in the 5' to 3' direction. The leading strand is synthesized continuously, while the lagging strand is synthesized in short fragments called Okazaki fragments. Both strands are synthesized in the 5' to 3' direction. So, DNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nC) RNA editing: RNA editing is a process that involves the modification of RNA molecules after transcription. This can include the insertion, deletion, or modification of nucleotides. RNA editing can occur in both 5' to 3' and 3' to 5' directions, depending on the specific editing event. So, RNA editing can occur in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nD) Transcription: Transcription is the process of synthesizing RNA from a DNA template. During transcription, the RNA polymerase enzyme reads the DNA template strand in the 3' to 5' direction and synthesizes the RNA strand in the 5' to 3' direction. So, transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nBased on our analysis, all of the processes listed (DNA repair, DNA replication, RNA editing, and transcription) can occur in the 5' to 3' direction. However, RNA editing is the only process that can also occur in the 3' to 5' direction, depending on the specific editing event. Therefore, the answer is:\n\nC) RNA editing",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a3035059-5ce4-4504-94ec-99609b2c2f00",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) RNA editing, as it is the only process that can also occur in the 3' to 5' direction, depending on the specific editing event.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/14 18:44:00",
