                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what 5' to 3' direction means. This means that we are looking at the DNA strand from the 5' end to the 3' end. \n\nNext, we need to understand what each of the processes listed in the question are. \n-DNA repair is the process of fixing damaged DNA. \n-DNA replication is the process of copying DNA. \n-RNA editing is the process of changing the sequence of RNA. \n-Transcription is the process of making RNA from DNA. \n\nNow that we understand the processes, we can figure out which one does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction. \n\nDNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction because that is the direction that DNA is copied. DNA repair can also occur in the 5' to 3' direction because that is the direction that DNA is read. RNA editing and transcription, however, do not occur in the 5' to 3' direction. RNA editing occurs in the 3' to 5' direction, and transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a043df29-cf14-4b87-afa4-ece965c8daaa",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " C- RNA Editing.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
