                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: C) RNA editing\n\nExplanation: DNA repair, DNA replication, and transcription all occur in the 5' to 3' direction. This means that the nucleotides are added to the 3' end of the growing strand. RNA editing, however, does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction. Instead, it occurs in the opposite direction, from 3' to 5'. This means that the nucleotides are added to the 5' end of the growing strand. Therefore, the correct answer is C) RNA editing.",
