                        "cot": " \n\nStep 1: Tetralogy of Fallot is a congenital heart defect. \n\nStep 2: When a person has a congenital heart defect, they need to be in a position that is comfortable and allows for the best circulation of blood. \n\nStep 3: The best position for a person with a congenital heart defect is the supine position, which is lying flat on the back. \n\nAnswer: A) Supine",
