                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nTetralogy of Fallot is a condition in which the child has a hole between the heart and the lungs. This causes the blood to flow back into the heart. The child will have trouble breathing and will need to be on a ventilator. The child will also have trouble eating and will need to be fed through a tube.\nThe child with tetralogy of fallot will need to be in a position that allows the blood to flow back into the heart. This will allow the child to breathe easier. The child will also need to be in a position that allows the child to eat.\nThe answer is D.",
