                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-10",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nFirst, the patient came with pain in calf muscles on exercise. This suggests that the pain is related to the muscles.\n\nSecond, on biopsy, excessive amount of glycogen was found. This suggests that there is a problem with glycogen metabolism.\n\nThird, the most likely enzyme deficiency is phosphofructokinase I. This enzyme is responsible for the metabolism of glycogen.",
                        "answers": [
