                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe excessive amount of glycogen in the muscle suggests a problem with glycogen metabolism. \n\nOption A: Muscle debranching enzyme deficiency would lead to the accumulation of abnormal glycogen structures, but not necessarily excessive amounts of glycogen. \n\nOption B: Phosphofructokinase I deficiency would lead to impaired glycolysis and decreased ATP production, but not necessarily glycogen accumulation. \n\nOption C: Glucose 6 phosphatase deficiency would lead to impaired gluconeogenesis and glycogenolysis, but not necessarily glycogen accumulation. \n\nOption D: Phosphorylase enzyme deficiency would lead to impaired glycogenolysis and the accumulation of glycogen in the muscle. \n\nTherefore, the most likely enzyme deficiency in this case is D) Phosphorylase enzyme.",
                        "answers": [
