                        "cot": "\n\nDifficult. \n\nThe excessive amount of glycogen in the muscle suggests a problem with glycogen metabolism. The most likely enzyme deficiency in this case is muscle phosphorylase enzyme, which is responsible for breaking down glycogen into glucose-1-phosphate. Deficiency of this enzyme leads to glycogen accumulation in the muscle, causing pain and weakness during exercise. Therefore, the answer is D) Phosphorylase enzyme.",
