 in gluconeogenesis and glycogenolysis, right? It converts glucose 6-phosphate to glucose.\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. If there was a deficiency in this enzyme, would it cause excessive glycogen to accumulate in the muscle?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure. It might, since glucose production from glycogen would be impaired.\n\nProfessor: However, glucose 6-phosph",
