                        "cot": "A) Posterior cruciate ligament - The positive pivot shift test is not typically associated with injury to the posterior cruciate ligament, so this option is unlikely to be correct.\n\nB) Anterior cruciate ligament - The positive pivot shift test is commonly associated with injury to the anterior cruciate ligament, so this option is a strong possibility.\n\nC) Medial meniscus - Injury to the medial meniscus can cause pain and other symptoms, but it is not typically associated with a positive pivot shift test, so this option is unlikely to be correct.\n\nD) Lateral meniscus - Injury to the lateral meniscus can cause pain and other symptoms, but it is not typically associated with a positive pivot shift test, so this option is unlikely to be correct.\n\nCombining all the information gathered, it seems that the correct answer is B) Anterior cruciate ligament.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) Anterior cruciate ligament.",
