                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking for the cause of a positive pivot shift test in the knee. We need to identify which of the given options is responsible for this test result.\n\nStep 2: Review the options\nA) Posterior cruciate ligament\nB) Anterior cruciate ligament\nC) Medial meniscus\nD) Lateral meniscus\n\nStep 3: Understand the pivot shift test\nThe pivot shift test is a clinical test used to assess the integrity of the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) in the knee. A positive pivot shift test indicates that there is an injury to the ACL, which is responsible for stabilizing the knee joint.\n\nStep 4: Match the correct option\nSince the pivot shift test is used to assess the integrity of the ACL, a positive test result would indicate an injury to the anterior cruciate ligament.\n\nStep 5: Answer the question\nPositive pivot shift test in knee is because of injury to -\nB) Anterior cruciate ligament",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "11733195-cd31-4387-b6e8-678b2c09da05",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
