                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the question and the options provided.\n\nQuestion: Where was there a lot more water vapor in the air during the trip?\n\nOptions: A) Hanoi, B) Athens, C) Baghdad, D) Phoenix\n\nStep 2: Consider the climate and geographical location of each option.\n\nA) Hanoi is located in Vietnam, which has a tropical climate with high humidity and rainfall.\n\nB) Athens is located in Greece, which has a Mediterranean climate with hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters.\n\nC) Baghdad is located in Iraq, which has a desert climate with hot, dry summers and cool, dry winters.\n\nD) Phoenix is located in Arizona, USA, which has a desert climate with hot, dry summers and mild winters.\n\nStep 3: Based on the climate and geographical location of each option, eliminate the options that are less likely to have a lot of water vapor in the air.\n\nElimination: Option B (Athens) and Option D (Phoenix) are less likely to have a lot of water vapor in the air because they have dry climates.\n\nStep 4: Compare the remaining options and choose the one that is most likely to have a lot of water vapor in the air.\n\nComparison: Option A (Hanoi) has a tropical climate with high humidity and rainfall, while Option C (Baghdad) has a desert climate with low humidity and rainfall.\n\nConclusion: Therefore, the answer is A) Hanoi, as it is most likely to have a lot more water vapor in the air during the trip.",
