                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine which city had more water vapor in the air during the trip, we need to consider the humidity levels in each city. Humidity is a measure of the amount of water vapor in the air. The higher the humidity, the more water vapor is present. \n\nAdditional facts:\n- Hanoi is the capital of Vietnam and has a tropical climate with high humidity levels.\n- Athens is the capital of Greece and has a Mediterranean climate with moderate humidity levels.\n- Baghdad is the capital of Iraq and has a desert climate with low humidity levels.\n- Phoenix is a city in Arizona, USA, and also has a desert climate with low humidity levels.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) What are the average humidity levels in each city?\n- Hanoi: The average humidity level in Hanoi is around 80%.\n- Athens: The average humidity level in Athens is around 60%.\n- Baghdad: The average humidity level in Baghdad is around 30%.\n- Phoenix: The average humidity level in Phoenix is around 25%.\n\n2) Which city has the highest average humidity level?\nBased on the information above, Hanoi has the highest average humidity level at 80%.\n\nAnswer: There was a lot more water vapor in the air when we went on a trip to Hanoi (A).",
