                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you repeat the question please?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the question is: Seals are most likely to be found in what type of environment?\n\nStudent: Okay, and what are the options?\n\nProfessor: The options are: A) desert, B) arctic, C) Mediterranean, and D) tropical.\n\nStudent: Hmm, I think I remember learning about this in class. Is it the arctic environment?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct! Seals are most commonly found in the arctic environment. They are adapted to living in cold water and on ice, which makes the arctic a perfect habitat for them.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. But what about the other options? Why are they not the right answer?\n\nProfessor: Well, seals are not typically found in desert environments because they need water to survive. The Mediterranean and tropical environments are too warm for them, and they are not adapted to living in those types of climates.\n\nStudent: Okay, that makes sense. Thank you for explaining it to me, professor.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome! It's always important to understand why certain answers are correct and why others are not.",
