                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: What is cellular respiration?\n\nProfessor: Cellular respiration is a process that cells use to convert energy from food into a usable form of energy called ATP.\n\nStudent: What are the steps of cellular respiration?\n\nProfessor: The steps of cellular respiration are glycolysis, the Krebs cycle, and electron transport.\n\nStudent: What is glycolysis?\n\nProfessor: Glycolysis is the first step of cellular respiration. In glycolysis, glucose is converted into pyruvate.\n\nStudent: What is the Krebs cycle?\n\nProfessor: The Krebs cycle is the second step of cellular respiration. In the Krebs cycle, pyruvate is converted into ATP.\n\nStudent: What is electron transport?\n\nProfessor: Electron transport is the third and final step of cellular respiration. In electron transport, ATP is produced from the energy released by the oxidation of pyruvate.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "cb21771b-36e3-46eb-be50-e2288d608d58",
