                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: D) Release Energy\n\nExplanation: \nCellular respiration is a process that occurs in all cells and is used to release energy from the breakdown of glucose molecules. This energy is used to power the cell's activities, such as synthesizing proteins, transporting molecules, and replicating DNA. Photosynthesis is a process used by plants and other photosynthetic organisms to convert light energy into chemical energy, which is then used to produce glucose molecules. Waste is released from cells as a byproduct of cellular respiration and other metabolic processes. Meiosis is a type of cell division that occurs in reproductive cells and is used to produce gametes, which are the cells used in sexual reproduction.",
