                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) Spider bites\n\nAnswer: Incorrect. Spider bites are not caused by medicine, but rather by the venom of a spider. Medicine can be used to treat the symptoms of a spider bite, but it does not cause them. \n\nB) Vomiting\n\nAnswer: Correct. Medicine can cause people to have allergic reactions such as vomiting. This is because some medicines contain ingredients that can irritate the stomach and cause nausea and vomiting. \n\nC) Placebo effect\n\nAnswer: Incorrect. The placebo effect is a psychological phenomenon in which a person's symptoms are relieved by taking a medication or treatment that has no active ingredients. It is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. \n\nD) Dance fever\n\nAnswer: Incorrect. Dance fever is not an allergic reaction caused by medicine. It is a term used to describe a feeling of excitement or enthusiasm for dancing.",
