                        "cot": "To work this out step by step, let's first understand the question. The question is asking what factor, through DNA, will cause a rabbit to have long ears. \n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Rabbits are born with ears: This statement is true, but it does not specifically address the length of the ears. So, this option is not the correct answer.\n\nB) There was a lot of food: The availability of food might affect the overall health and growth of a rabbit, but it does not directly determine the length of a rabbit's ears through DNA. So, this option is not the correct answer.\n\nC) Genetic contributors had long ears: This option directly addresses the DNA factor. If the genetic contributors (i.e., the parents or ancestors) of a rabbit had long ears, it is more likely that the rabbit will also have long ears due to the inheritance of genes. So, this option seems to be the correct answer.\n\nD) Parents were also rabbits: This statement is true, but it does not specifically address the length of the ears. So, this option is not the correct answer.\n\nBased on the analysis of each option, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Genetic contributors had long ears.",
