                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Through DNA, a rabbit will have long ears if which of the following is true?\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n- DNA is the genetic material that determines the traits of an organism.\n- Traits are inherited from parents through the combination of their DNA.\n- Rabbits are mammals, and their traits, such as ear length, are determined by their genetics.\n- Environmental factors, such as food availability, can influence the expression of certain traits, but they do not directly determine the genetic makeup of an organism.\n\nSub-questions and answers:\n1) Do rabbits need to be born with ears to have long ears?\n- No, being born with ears is a given for rabbits, but it does not determine the length of their ears.\n\n2) Does the availability of food determine if a rabbit will have long ears?\n- No, while food availability can influence the expression of certain traits, it does not directly determine the genetic makeup of an organism, such as ear length.\n\n3) Do genetic contributors with long ears determine if a rabbit will have long ears?\n- Yes, if the genetic contributors (parents) have long ears, it is more likely that the rabbit will inherit the genes responsible for long ears.\n\n4) Do parents need to be rabbits for a rabbit to have long ears?\n- Yes, parents need to be rabbits for the offspring to be a rabbit, but this does not directly determine the length of the offspring's ears.\n\nAnswer to the original question: Through DNA, a rabbit will have long ears if genetic contributors had long ears (option C).",
