                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nQ: Through DNA, a rabbit will have long ears if:\n\nA) rabbits are born with ears\nB) there was a lot of food\nC) genetic contributors had long ears\nD) parents were also rabbits\n\nA) rabbits are born with ears - This is not correct. All animals are born with ears, but the length of the ears is determined by DNA.\n\nB) there was a lot of food - This is not correct. The amount of food has no bearing on the length of a rabbit's ears.\n\nC) genetic contributors had long ears - This is correct. The length of a rabbit's ears is determined by the genes it inherits from its parents. If the parents have long ears, the rabbit is likely to have long ears as well.\n\nD) parents were also rabbits - This is correct. The length of a rabbit's ears is determined by the genes it inherits from its parents. If the parents have long ears, the rabbit is likely to have long ears as well.",
