                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) genetic contributors had long ears.\n\nTo explain why this is the correct answer, we must first understand how DNA works. DNA is a molecule that contains genetic information that is passed from parent to offspring. This genetic information is responsible for the physical characteristics of an organism, such as the length of its ears.\n\nTherefore, in order for a rabbit to have long ears, the genetic contributors (i.e. the parents) must have long ears. This is because the genetic information from the parents is passed on to the offspring, and this genetic information is responsible for the physical characteristics of the offspring.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) genetic contributors had long ears.",
