                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe original question is: Through DNA, a rabbit will have long ears if...\n\nTo answer this question, it is important to understand the basics of genetics and how DNA is passed from parent to offspring. DNA is a molecule that contains the instructions for the development and functioning of living organisms. It is passed from parent to offspring through the process of reproduction.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How is DNA passed from parent to offspring?\n2. How does DNA determine the physical characteristics of an organism?\n\nAnswer to sub-question 1: DNA is passed from parent to offspring through the process of reproduction.\n\nAnswer to sub-question 2: DNA determines the physical characteristics of an organism by providing instructions for the development and functioning of the organism.\n\nAnswer to original question: Through DNA, a rabbit will have long ears if genetic contributors had long ears (Option C). This is because the DNA of the genetic contributors will be passed on to the offspring, which will determine the physical characteristics of the offspring, including the length of its ears.",
