                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what happens when resources decrease in an environment?\n\nProfessor: Sure, when resources decrease in an environment, organisms have to adapt to the change. One possible response is to use more of their resources.\n\nStudent: So, does that mean the answer is A?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. A is the answer.\n\nStudent: Okay, but why do organisms use more of their resources when resources decrease?\n\nProfessor: Well, when resources are scarce, organisms need to use more of their resources to survive. For example, if there is less food available, an animal might need to eat more of it to get the energy it needs.\n\nStudent: I see. But wouldn't using more resources lead to even more scarcity?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's a good point. Using more resources can lead to a vicious cycle of scarcity. That's why some organisms might respond to resource scarcity by being more economical with their resources.\n\nStudent: So, is the answer D then?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. D is the answer. When resources decrease, organisms might become more economical with their resources to avoid further scarcity.",
