                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, let's first understand the context. The question is about how organisms respond to a decrease in resources in their environment.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) induces organisms to use more of their resources\n- This option suggests that when resources are decreasing, organisms will use more of their resources. This doesn't make sense because if resources are already scarce, using more of them would only worsen the situation for the organisms.\n\nB) causes an increase in use of resources\n- This option is similar to option A, suggesting that organisms will use more resources when they are scarce. Again, this doesn't make sense because using more resources when they are already scarce would only worsen the situation for the organisms.\n\nC) causes an uptick in birthrate\n- This option suggests that when resources are scarce, organisms will reproduce more. This doesn't make sense because when resources are limited, it would be difficult for organisms to support more offspring. In fact, in many cases, a decrease in resources can lead to a decrease in birthrate as organisms struggle to survive and reproduce.\n\nD) induces organisms to be more economical with resources\n- This option suggests that when resources are scarce, organisms will try to use them more efficiently and sparingly. This makes sense because when resources are limited, organisms need to adapt their behavior to ensure their survival. By being more economical with resources, organisms can make the limited resources last longer and increase their chances of survival.\n\nBased on the analysis of each option, the correct answer is:\n\nD) induces organisms to be more economical with resources",
