                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm having trouble understanding this multiple-choice question about resources decreasing in an environment. Can you help me work through it?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option one by one and see if it makes sense. The first option is A) induces organisms to use more of their resources. What do you think about this one?\n\nStudent: Well, if resources are decreasing, it doesn't seem logical for organisms to use more of their resources. Wouldn't they want to conserve them?\n\nProfessor: That's correct! So we can eliminate option A. Now let's look at option B) causes an increase in use of resources. What are your thoughts on this one?\n\nStudent: This option seems similar to option A. If resources are decreasing, it doesn't make sense for there to be an increase in the use of resources.\n\nProfessor: Exactly, so we can eliminate option B as well. Now let's consider option C) causes an uptick in birthrate. What do you think about this one?\n\nStudent: I'm not sure about this one. I can see how a decrease in resources might cause organisms to reproduce more to ensure their survival, but I can also see how it might cause them to reproduce less because there are fewer resources to support offspring.\n\nProfessor: That's a good point. However, in general, when resources are scarce, organisms tend to focus on their own survival rather than reproducing. So, we can eliminate option C. Finally, let's look at option D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources. What are your thoughts on this one?\n\nStudent: This option seems to make the most sense. If resources are decreasing, organisms would want to be more careful with how they use their resources to ensure their survival.\n\nProfessor: That's correct! So, the correct answer is D) induces organisms to be more economical with resources. Does that make sense to you?\n\nStudent: Yes, it does. Thank you for helping me work through the question, Professor!",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "1aa71ed2-d628-48ae-b193-335f78cd8f2d",
