                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: I'm not sure about the answer to this question. Can you help me understand why Bill planted rapeseed one year and soybeans the next?\n\nProfessor: Of course! This is a practice called crop rotation. Farmers do this to maintain soil fertility and reduce pests and diseases. Let's go through the options one by one to find the right answer.\n\nStudent: Okay, let's start with option A.\n\nProfessor: Option A is \"get bigger yields.\" Crop rotation can indeed lead to bigger yields because it helps maintain soil fertility and reduces pests and diseases. So, this is a possible answer.\n\nStudent: What about option B?\n\nProfessor: Option B is \"make things boring.\" This doesn't make sense in the context of farming. Farmers are more concerned with productivity and sustainability than making things boring. So, we can eliminate this option.\n\nStudent: Alright, how about option C?\n\nProfessor: Option C is \"keep things random.\" While crop rotation does involve changing the crops planted each year, it's not done randomly. It's a carefully planned process to ensure the best results for the soil and crops. So, this option is not correct either.\n\nStudent: That leaves us with option D.\n\nProfessor: Option D is \"get smaller yields.\" This is the opposite of what crop rotation aims to achieve. As we discussed earlier, crop rotation helps maintain soil fertility and reduce pests and diseases, which can lead to bigger yields. So, this option is not correct.\n\nStudent: So, the correct answer is option A, \"get bigger yields.\"\n\nProfessor: That's correct! By practicing crop rotation, Bill is able to maintain soil fertility and reduce pests and diseases, which can lead to bigger yields. Well done!",
