                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA) get bigger yields\n\nComplementary Knowledge: Rapeseed and soybeans are both legumes, meaning they are nitrogen-fixing plants that can help improve soil fertility.\n\nSub-Questions:\n1. What are the yields of rapeseed and soybeans?\n2. How does planting different crops help increase yields?\n\nAnswer:\nA) get bigger yields\n\nExplanation: Planting different crops helps increase yields because it prevents soil depletion and allows for the replenishment of nutrients. Rapeseed and soybeans are both legumes, meaning they are nitrogen-fixing plants that can help improve soil fertility. This means that planting different crops in the same field can help increase yields by replenishing the soil with nutrients.",
