                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine the best way for a frog to get warm, let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Wear a Christmas sweater: Frogs are cold-blooded animals, which means they rely on their environment to regulate their body temperature. Wearing a sweater might help a mammal stay warm, but it would not be effective for a frog since they don't produce their own body heat.\n\nB) Drink a hot chocolate: Frogs do not consume food or drink in the same way humans do. They primarily eat insects and other small animals, and they absorb water through their skin. Drinking hot chocolate would not be an effective way for a frog to warm up.\n\nC) Go for a run: While physical activity can generate heat in mammals, frogs are not built for long-distance running. Additionally, since they are cold-blooded, their body temperature is dependent on their environment, so running would not necessarily help them warm up.\n\nD) Sit under a lamp: This option seems the most plausible for a frog to get warm. As cold-blooded animals, frogs rely on external heat sources to regulate their body temperature. Sitting under a lamp would provide the necessary heat for a frog to warm up.\n\nBased on this analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Sit under a lamp",
