                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: Which of these will make a frog warm?\n\nProfessor: Well, let's think about it. What do we know about frogs?\n\nStudent: They're cold-blooded.\n\nProfessor: That's right. So, they can't generate their own body heat.\n\nStudent: So, they would need something to make them warm from the outside.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. Now, let's look at our options. Wearing a Christmas sweater would probably not do the trick because it's not generating heat, it's just trapping body heat that the frog already has.\n\nStudent: Okay.\n\nProfessor: Drinking a hot chocolate would also not work because, again, it's not generating heat.\n\nStudent: Right.\n\nProfessor: Going for a run would also not work because, while it would generate heat, it would also make the frog move around and use up that heat.\n\nStudent: I see.\n\nProfessor: So, that leaves us with option D, sitting under a lamp. A lamp produces heat, so that would make the frog warm.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Thanks for explaining it.",
                        "answers": [
