                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nThe first step is to identify the key words in the question. In this case, the key words are \"worms,\" \"nutrients,\" \"dead organisms,\" and \"soil.\" \n\nThe second step is to think about what each of these key words mean. \n\nWorms are small, slimy creatures that live in the ground. They eat dead leaves and other things that fall to the ground. \n\nNutrients are things that plants need to grow, like water and sunlight. \n\nDead organisms are things that used to be alive, but are now dead. \n\nSoil is the dirt that plants grow in. \n\nThe third step is to put the information from the key words together to form a sentence. In this case, the sentence would be something like, \"Worms help to put nutrients from dead organisms back into the soil.\" \n\nThe fourth step is to look at the answer choices and see which one best matches the sentence that you created. In this case, the best answer would be \"C) recycling.\"",
