                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To see how wind affects sand, we need to observe the movement and patterns of sand particles in response to wind. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What tools or methods can we use to observe sand movement?\n2. How does wind speed and direction affect sand movement?\n3. What are the different types of sand formations that can be created by wind?\n\n1. To observe sand movement, we can use tools such as anemometers to measure wind speed, and cameras or time-lapse photography to capture the movement of sand particles over time. \n2. Wind speed and direction can greatly affect sand movement. Strong winds can cause sand to be lifted and carried away, while weaker winds may only cause small ripples or patterns in the sand. The direction of the wind can also determine the direction of sand movement. \n3. Wind can create various types of sand formations, such as sand dunes, ripples, and drifts. Sand dunes are created by wind carrying sand particles and depositing them in a specific area, while ripples and drifts are created by the movement of sand particles along the ground. \n\nTherefore, to see how wind affects sand, we can observe the movement and patterns of sand particles using tools such as anemometers and cameras, and take into account the speed and direction of the wind, as well as the different types of sand formations that can be created.",
