                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A, B, C, and D are all helpful knowledge and additional facts, but the answer to the original question is not explicitly stated in them. The answer is: To see how wind affects sand, we can observe the movement and patterns of sand particles using tools such as anemometers and cameras, and take into account the speed and direction of the wind, as well as the different types of sand formations that can be created.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
