                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To see how wind affects sand, we can start by examining the properties of sand and how it interacts with wind. \n\nSand is made up of small, loose particles that can be easily moved by external forces such as wind. When wind blows over a surface covered with sand, it can pick up and move the sand particles, causing them to shift and create various patterns and formations. \n\nNow, let's look at the answer choices:\n\nA) Sand is always moving: This statement is not entirely accurate, as sand can be stationary when there is no external force acting upon it. However, it is true that sand can be easily moved by forces such as wind.\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand: This statement is true. Sandstorms are caused by strong winds that pick up and move sand particles, creating ripples and other patterns in the sand. This is a visible effect of wind on sand.\n\nC) Sand is easy to move through: This statement is not directly related to the effect of wind on sand. While it is true that sand can be easy to move through, this does not necessarily show how wind affects sand.\n\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand: This statement is true and can be related to the effect of wind on sand. The waves in the sand at beaches are often caused by wind blowing over the surface, moving the sand particles and creating patterns. This is another visible effect of wind on sand.\n\nBased on the analysis of the answer choices, the best answers to show how wind affects sand are B) Sandstorms create ripples in sand and D) Beaches often have waves in the sand. These two options demonstrate visible effects of wind on sand, showing how the movement of sand particles can create patterns and formations.",
