                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question to make sure we understand it correctly: How can we observe the effects of wind on sand?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step: \nA) Sand is always moving - This is true, but it is not necessarily a direct result of wind. Sand can be moved by other forces such as water or gravity.\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand - This is true, and it is a direct result of wind. Wind can cause sand to move and create ripples in the sand.\n\nC) Sand is easy to move through - This is true, but it is not necessarily a direct result of wind. Sand can be moved by other forces such as water or gravity.\n\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand - This is true, and it is a direct result of wind. Wind can cause sand to move and create waves in the sand.\n\nThird, let's make sure we have the right answer: The correct answer is B) Sandstorms create ripples in sand and D) Beaches often have waves in the sand, as these are direct results of wind.",
