                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nTo answer this question, we need to understand how wind affects sand. Wind is a force that can move particles, like sand, and cause them to shift and move.\n\nA) Sand is always moving: This is true. Wind can cause sand to move, but it is also affected by other forces, such as gravity and water.\n\nB) Sandstorms create ripples in sand: This is also true. Sandstorms are caused by strong winds, which can cause the sand to move and create ripples in the sand.\n\nC) Sand is easy to move through: This is true. Sand is made up of small particles, which makes it easy for wind to move it around.\n\nD) Beaches often have waves in the sand: This is true. Wind can cause waves in the sand, which can be seen on beaches.\n\nTo see how wind affects sand, we can observe sand on a beach or in a desert. We can observe how the wind causes the sand to move and create ripples or waves. We can also observe how the wind can cause sandstorms, which can cause large amounts of sand to move and create ripples in the sand.",
