                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A Punnett square is a tool used to predict the probability of an offspring inheriting a specific trait from its parents. It is based on the principles of Mendelian inheritance, which states that traits are determined by pairs of genes, with one gene inherited from each parent. \n\nTo answer this question, let's go through each option:\n\nA) Mother - A Punnett square cannot be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's mother because the mother is the one who passes the trait to the offspring, not the other way around.\n\nB) Grandfather - A Punnett square cannot be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's grandfather because the grandfather is the one who passes the trait to the parent, not the other way around.\n\nC) Daughter - A Punnett square can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's daughter. This is because the Punnett square is designed to predict the probability of an offspring (in this case, the daughter) inheriting a specific trait from its parents.\n\nD) Father - A Punnett square cannot be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's father because the father is the one who passes the trait to the offspring, not the other way around.\n\nBased on this reasoning, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Daughter",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "73fbb058-758c-42e3-b058-69e5c6ce623a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
