                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A Punnett square is a diagram that is used to predict the genotypes of a particular cross or breeding experiment. It is named after Reginald C. Punnett, who devised the approach. The diagram is used by biologists to determine the probability of an offspring having a particular genotype. The Punnett square is a visual representation of Mendelian inheritance.\n\nThe original question asks which family member's traits can be calculated using a Punnett square. To answer this question, we need to consider the following sub-questions:\n\n1. How does a Punnett square work?\n2. Which family members' traits can be predicted using a Punnett square?\n\n1. How does a Punnett square work?\nA Punnett square works by considering the possible combinations of alleles (versions of a gene) that can be inherited from each parent. Each parent contributes one allele for a specific trait to their offspring. The Punnett square is a grid that shows all possible combinations of alleles that can result from the cross of the two parents. By analyzing the grid, we can determine the probability of an offspring inheriting a specific trait.\n\n2. Which family members' traits can be predicted using a Punnett square?\nA Punnett square can be used to predict the traits of an offspring resulting from the combination of alleles from both parents. Therefore, it can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's child.\n\nNow, we can answer the original question:\n\nA Punnett square can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's\nA) mother - Incorrect, as a Punnett square is used to predict offspring traits, not parental traits.\nB) grandfather - Incorrect, as a Punnett square is used to predict offspring traits, not grandparent traits.\nC) daughter - Correct, as a Punnett square can be used to predict the traits of an offspring, which includes a daughter.\nD) father - Incorrect, as a Punnett square is used to predict offspring traits, not parental traits.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f33efae4-5ab5-45f3-a3c5-320a690acf9b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) daughter.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
