                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe answer is D) father.\n\nTo explain why, we need to understand how Punnett squares work. Punnett squares are used to calculate the probability of an offspring inheriting a certain trait from its parents. The Punnett square is a grid that shows all the possible combinations of alleles (genetic information) that can be inherited from the parents. Each parent contributes one allele to the offspring, and the Punnett square shows all the possible combinations of these alleles.\n\nFor example, if a father has the allele for brown eyes (B) and the mother has the allele for blue eyes (b), then the Punnett square would look like this:\n\nFather: B\nMother: b\n\nB  b\nB  Bb\nb  Bb\n\nIn this example, the offspring has a 50% chance of inheriting the allele for brown eyes (B) from the father, and a 50% chance of inheriting the allele for blue eyes (b) from the mother.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is D) father, because the Punnett square is used to calculate the probability of an offspring inheriting a certain trait from its father.",
                        "answers": [
