                    {
                        "id": "67f37800-e3d2-488a-bcdf-53ad570a35f9",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nA Punnett square is a tool used to calculate the probability of an offspring inheriting a certain trait from its parents. It is based on Mendelian genetics, which states that each parent contributes one allele (a form of a gene) to the offspring.\n\nA) mother: The mother contributes one allele to the offspring, so the chance of the trait being passed to the mother is 50%.\n\nB) grandfather: The grandfather does not contribute any alleles to the offspring, so the chance of the trait being passed to the grandfather is 0%.\n\nC) daughter: The daughter receives one allele from the